thing you need to know about the California primary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Ever since President Trump’s election, California has fashioned itself as a kind of center of the resistance to his administration. With Democrats overwhelmingly controlling both houses of the State Legislature, lawmakers here have looked for every opportunity to counter the White House. But California is also home to a reliable bastion of centrist voters, particularly in Orange County and the Central Valley.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/02/us/02votecatoday/merlin_169677981_84e84fb3-a3fb-4de0-a721-c047cb2002a5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 363, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/02/us/02votecatoday/merlin_169677981_84e84fb3-a3fb-4de0-a721-c047cb2002a5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 363}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/02/us/02votecatoday/merlin_169677981_84e84fb3-a3fb-4de0-a721-c047cb2002a5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 620, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/02/us/02votecatoday/merlin_169677981_84e84fb3-a3fb-4de0-a721-c047cb2002a5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1240, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/02/us/02votecatoday/merlin_169677981_84e84fb3-a3fb-4de0-a721-c047cb2002a5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/02/us/02votecatoday/merlin_169677981_84e84fb3-a3fb-4de0-a721-c047cb2002a5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thu