, 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Letters', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/2acd7c5c-b896-5571-9d47-dfb4babd9ba2', 'word_count': 878, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2acd7c5c-b896-5571-9d47-dfb4babd9ba2'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court will decide on yet another bid to curtail women’s rights masquerading as a safety measure.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/02/opinion/trumps-high-court-hears-its-first-abortion-case.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court will decide on yet another bid to curtail women’s rights masquerading as a safety measure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Louisiana, with nearly one million women of reproductive age, now has only three abortion clinics. A woman who chooses to have an abortion —\xa0as about a quarter of American women do — must make her way to one of those facilities, where she will be legally required to sit through counseling intended to discourage her from having the procedure as well as an ultrasound that must be shown and described in detail to her. She then must wait at least 24 hours before returning to the clinic for the procedure. If she is a Medicaid patient, her bill will most likely be hundreds of dollars paid out of pocket.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/02/opinion/02abortion_illo/02abortion_illo-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/02/opinion/02abortion_illo/02abortion_illo-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/02/opinion/02abortion_illo/02abortion_illo-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'wi