one another than ever.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/02/theater/matthew-broderick-sarah-jessica-parker-plaza-suite.html', 'snippet': 'In Neil Simon’s “Plaza Suite,” they are playing three different couples — and are seeing more of one another than ever.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One morning in January, Sarah Jessica Parker and Matthew Broderick found themselves together on the Upper East Side, close to a luncheonette they used to love, with an hour to spare. Parker couldn’t recall the name of the spot, but she did remember that 20 years earlier, Broderick had told her that it was the one from Robert Redford’s C.I.A. lunch run in “Three Days of the Condor,” and that shared memory was enough to navigate them to the door of the Lexington Candy Shop. “I never see you two together,” the gentleman running the place said. “I see you, and I see you.” But Matthew Broderick and Sarah Jessica Parker, showbiz couple, are an elusive sight in New York City.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/08/arts/08parker-broderick1/08parker-broderick1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/08/arts/08parker-broderick1/08parker-broderick1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/08/arts/08parker-broderick1/08parker-broderick1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/08/arts/08parker-broderick1/08parker-broderick1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'sub