stop bleeding.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/02/26/magazine/26atwar-mosul5/26atwar-mosul5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/02/26/magazine/26atwar-mosul5/26atwar-mosul5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/02/26/magazine/26atwar-mosul5/26atwar-mosul5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/02/26/magazine/26atwar-mosul5/26atwar-mosul5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 1200, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/02/26/magazine/26atwar-mosul5/26atwar-mosul5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/02/26/magazine/26atwar-mosul5/26atwar-mosul5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/02/26/magazine/26atwar-mosul5/26atwar-mosul5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'I Went to Iraq to Take Photographs. I Stayed On as a Medic.', 'kicker': 'At war', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civilian Casualties', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nursing and Nurses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mosul (Iraq)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-03T10:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Kay Potter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': 'Kay', 'lastname': 'Potter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32592cd9-f2ff-5814-96eb-6c4ee1ee289c', 'word_count': 1683, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32592cd9-f2ff-5814-96eb-6c4ee1ee289c'}, {'abstract': 'Magazine tear sheets and personal photos have been replaced by color-coordinated collage kits.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/03/style/collage-kits.html', 'snippet': 'Magazine tear sheets and personal photos have been replaced by color-coordinated collage kits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The wall behind Sierra Palantino’s bed is covered with photographs: a bushel of coral- and pearl-colored roses; a bouquet of ruby and pink Mylar balloons; a close-up of a neon sign that says, “all the feels.” In thousands of bedrooms around the world, the same pictures are arranged in a neat collage.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/05/fashion/03COLLAGEKITS1/merlin_169711398_b373eed0-4bcd-4c63-9ea6-be0b97bd271a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/05/fashion/03COLLAGEKITS1/merlin_169711398_b373eed0-4bcd-4c63-9ea6-be0b97bd271a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image'