0/03/03/us/politics/super-tuesday-primary-winners.html', 'snippet': 'The voting on the biggest day of the Democratic presidential campaign increasingly suggested a two-person race between candidates representing competing wings of the party.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Democratic presidential race emerged from Super Tuesday with two clear front-runners as Joseph R. Biden Jr. won Texas, Virginia, North Carolina and at least six other states, largely through support from African-Americans and moderates, while Senator Bernie Sanders harnessed the backing of liberals and young voters to claim the biggest prize of the campaign, California, and several other primaries.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Biden Revives Campaign, Winning Nine States, but Sanders Takes California', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Big Night for Biden Serves Notice to Sanders', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanders, Bernard', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2020', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endorsements', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warren, Elizabeth', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klobuchar, Amy', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-04T01:37:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': '