uding New England’s tallest building.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/04/arts/henry-cobb-dead.html', 'snippet': 'He was I.M. Pei’s unsung partner for nearly four decades but was responsible for a celebrated body of work in his own right, including New England’s tallest building.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Henry N. Cobb, who in 70 years as an architect — more than half of them in partnership with I.M. Pei — designed some of the country’s most prominent buildings, including Boston’s blue-glass John Hancock Tower, the tallest building in New England, died on Monday at his home in Manhattan. He was 93.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/05/obituaries/04cobb1/merlin_169979709_f47ba0ff-8581-43a7-809e-4d1ef9f98bea-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 748, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/05/obituaries/04cobb1/merlin_169979709_f47ba0ff-8581-43a7-809e-4d1ef9f98bea-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 748}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/05/obituaries/04cobb1/merlin_169979709_f47ba0ff-8581-43a7-809e-4d1ef9f98bea-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 822, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/05/obituaries/04cobb1/merlin_169979709_f47ba0ff-8581-43a7-809e-4d1ef9f98bea-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1644, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/05/obituaries/04cobb1/04cobb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbna