'word_count': 1405, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e2f0c79-1d5b-55dd-a6c3-52d41b8f579c'}, {'abstract': 'The peace agreement has left American veterans with mixed feelings — relief that U.S. forces are coming home and uncertainty about what the deal means for the Afghan people.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/05/magazine/05atwar-afghan-peace-deal-veterans.html', 'snippet': 'The peace agreement has left American veterans with mixed feelings — relief that U.S. forces are coming home and uncertainty about what the deal means for the Afghan people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Saturday, the United States and the Taliban signed a historic peace agreement, theoretically bringing to an end the nearly two-decades-long conflict in Afghanistan that killed more than more than 2,400 American service members. As officials prepare to implement the terms of that deal, American veterans who served in the country are left to grapple with the provisions that may result in more uncertainty than stability for the people of Afghanistan they once fought to protect.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/08/23/world/00afghan-photos-2013b-copy/23afghanphotos_ss-slide-PCXJ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/08/23/world/00afghan-photos-2013b-copy/23afghanphotos_ss-slide-PCXJ-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/08/23/world/00afghan-photos-2013b-copy/23afghanphotos_ss-slide-PCXJ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/08/23/world/00afghan-photos-2013b-copy/23afghanphotos_ss-slide-PCXJ-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/08/23/world/00afghan-photos-2013b-copy/23afghanphotos_ss-slide-PCXJ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/08/23/world/00afghan-photos-2013b-copy/23afghanphotos_ss-slide-PCXJ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/08/23/world/00afghan-photos-2013b-copy/23afghanphotos_ss-slide-PCXJ-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After Tours in Afghanistan, U.S. Veterans Weigh Peace With the Taliban', 'kicker': 'At war', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Afghanistan Tours,  U.S. Veterans Appraise  Peace Deal With Taliban', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Afghan National Security Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Iraq and Afghanistan Veterans of America', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-05T10:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Ismay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ismay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb363a6a-4d3f-57dc-9247-34c6c85bc06e', 'word_count': 1529, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb363a6a-4d3f-57dc-9247-34c6c85bc06e'}, {'abstract': 'ICE is boosting its operations in sanctuary cities to arrest and deport undocumented immigrants, conducting round-the-clock surveillance in addition to deploying elite tactical agents.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/05/us/ICE-BORTAC-sanctuary-cities.html', 'snippet': 'ICE is boosting its operations in sanctuary cities to arrest and deport undocumented immigrants, conducting round-the-clock surveillance in addition to deploying elite tactical agents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Intensifying its enforcement in so-called sanctuary cities across the country, Immigration and Customs Enforcement has begun 24-hour-a-day surveillance operations around the homes and workplaces of undocumented immigrants. The agency plans to deploy hundreds of additional officers in unmarked cars in the coming weeks to increase arrests in cities where local law enforcement agencies do not cooperate with federal immigration enforcement.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/05/us/05ice-ops01/merlin_170016546_cb267a22-c788-47c0-a787-c388639a0c17-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/05/us/05ice-ops01/merlin_170016546_cb267a22-c788-47c0-a787-c388639a0c17-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/05/us/05ice-ops01/merlin_170016546_cb267a22-c788-47c0-a787-c388639a0c17-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'wid