 of his family’s venerable glass works corporation to serve for two decades as a wealthy congressman from upstate New York, becoming a leading moderate Republican voice who defied his party’s hard-right turn, died on Wednesday at his home in Corning, N.Y. He was 93.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/06/obituaries/06houghton1/merlin_170062653_90be5ac9-5b69-4eda-aa28-2d2b11ac6e63-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 514, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/06/obituaries/06houghton1/merlin_170062653_90be5ac9-5b69-4eda-aa28-2d2b11ac6e63-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 514}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/06/obituaries/06houghton1/merlin_170062653_90be5ac9-5b69-4eda-aa28-2d2b11ac6e63-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 877, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/06/obituaries/06houghton1/merlin_170062653_90be5ac9-5b69-4eda-aa28-2d2b11ac6e63-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1754, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/06/obituaries/06houghton1/05houghton1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/06/obituaries/06houghton1/05houghton1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/06/obituaries/06houghton1/05houghton1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Amory Houghton Jr., Who Went From Corning to Congress, Dies at 93', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Amory Houghton Jr.,  Congressman Who Came  From Corning, Dies at 93', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Houghton, Amory Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Glassware', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Corning Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Corning (NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-05T20:03:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Obits', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph P. Fried', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': 'P.', 'lastname': 'Fried', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/90993a93-9e9c-5a73-941e-ec03b6f42859', 'word_count': 1155, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90993a93-9e9c-5a73-941e-ec03b6f42859'}, {'abstract': "From Leila Chatti's series of poems that brilliantly explores the trauma of extreme illness.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/05/magazine/poem-waking-after-the-surgery.html', 'snippet': "From Leila Chatti's series of poems that brilliantly explores the trauma of extreme illness.", 'lead_paragraph': 'To write a series of poems out of extreme illness is a bracing accomplishment indeed. In “Deluge,” her first full-length book, Leila Chatti, born of a Catholic mother and a Muslim father, brilliantly explores the trauma. In a frightening two-year saga of a tumor and the “flooding” it caused, Chatti finds not disassociation but deeper association with her own experience. Her strikingly personal relationship with Mary — who appears in both the Quran and the Bible — becomes a profound and steadying compass, as do lines from many other poets and philosophers, woven into the text in cento style. Selected by Naomi Shihab Nye', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/08/magazine/08mag-poem-1/08mag-poem-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 188, 'width': 293, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/08/magazine/08mag-poem-1/08mag-poem-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 188, 'width': 293, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/08/magazine/08mag-poem-1/08mag-poem-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/08/magazine/08mag-poem-1/08mag-poem-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/08/magazine/08mag-poem-1/08mag-poem-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Poem: Waking After the Surgery', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-05T20:04:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leila Chatti and Naomi Shihab Nye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leila', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chatti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Naomi', 'middlename': 'Shihab', 'lastname': 'Nye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03342145-e4f4-5eff-a4dc-ff31d3fd610e', 'word_count': 250, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03342145-e4f4-5eff-a4dc-ff31d3fd610e'}, {'abstract': 'The crisis is forcing a tech boomtown to hit pause.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/05/opinion/coronavirus-seattle.html', 'snippet': 'The crisis is forcing a tech boomtown to hit pause.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEATTLE — There is a strange in-betweenness to life in the nation’s coronavirus capital. Classes continue on the University of Washington’s campus, some half-empty, others completely full. I have been teaching here 13 years, and faculty members have been getting detailed, palpably anxious instructions from administrators on how to teach online and on hand-washing and social distance, and reminders that no one on our 46,000-student campus has tested positive for the coronavirus that causes Covid-19. For now.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/05/opinion/05Omara2/merlin_170068041_6b4bc884-d187-4868-b794-a016eabf8cd2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/05/opinion/05Omara2/merlin_170068041_6b4bc884-d187-4868-b794-a016eabf8cd2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/0