s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Henri Richard, the Montreal Canadiens’ Hall of Fame center who played on an N.H.L.-record 11 Stanley Cup winners and skated alongside his brother Maurice the Rocket when the Canadiens ruled hockey in the 1950s as the Flying Frenchmen, died on Friday in Laval, Quebec. He was 84.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/07/obituaries/07Richard-obit1/06Richard1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 765, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/07/obituaries/07Richard-obit1/06Richard1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 765}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/07/obituaries/07Richard-obit1/06Richard1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 803, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/07/obituaries/07Richard-obit1/06Richard1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1606, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/07/obituaries/07Richard-obit1/06Richard1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/07/obituaries/07Richard-obit1/06Richard1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/07/obituaries/07Richard-obit1/06Richard1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Henri Richard, Hall of Fame Center for Montreal Canadiens, Dies at 84', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Henri Richard, Hall of Fame Center for Montreal Canadiens, Is Dead at 84', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Richard, Henri (1936-2020)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Montreal Canadiens', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stanley Cup', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-06T17:31:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Obits', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Goldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/8bdf0a2f-72cb-55e9-9106-6d325425c418', 'word_count': 1073, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8bdf0a2f-72cb-55e9-9106-6d325425c418'}, {'abstract': 'For Melissa Clark, the food she grew up eating in Brooklyn, and the French cuisine her parents adored, laid the foundation for how she still cooks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/06/dining/dinner-in-french-book-melissa-clark.html', 'snippet': 'For Melissa Clark, the food she grew up eating in Brooklyn, and the French cuisine her parents adored, laid the foundation for how she still cooks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I can’t really speak French, but I cook in French. For years, I studied conjugations and the passé simple, practiced pronouncing yaourt and grenouille, but try as I might I just couldn’t seem to master it beyond the essentials like “deux pains au chocolat, s’il vous plaît.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'ran