, {'abstract': 'On a set that transforms the Bushwick Starr into a cave beneath a tree, Jillian Walker tells a story of her family, and of blackness in America, that aches with hope.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/06/theater/skinfolk-review.html', 'snippet': 'On a set that transforms the Bushwick Starr into a cave beneath a tree, Jillian Walker tells a story of her family, and of blackness in America, that aches with hope.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “Strange Fruit,” Billie Holiday’s protest song from 1939, the jazz singer evoked the gruesome imagery that haunted her: black bodies hanging from trees after being lynched by angry white mobs. Originally written by Abel Meeropol, Holiday’s rendition became an anthem of sorrow and anger, but from its endless pain also emanated a soulful wish, that the spirits of these wronged bodies would find solace in the world to come.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/03/arts/03skinfolk1/merlin_169706631_f9495d90-0066-4a0f-8365-d249e90d68a0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/03/arts/03skinfolk1/merlin_169706631_f9495d90-0066-4a0f-8365-d249e90d68a0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/03/arts/03skinfolk1/merlin_169706631_f9495d90-0066-4a0f-8365-d249e90d68a0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/03/arts/03skinfolk1/merlin_169706631_f9495d90-0066-4a0f-8365-d249e90d68a0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1333, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/03/arts/03skinfolk1/03skinfolk1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/03/arts/03skinfolk1/03skinfolk1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/03/arts/03skinfolk1/03skinfolk1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: In ‘Skinfolk,’ the Joys of Blackness Burst From the Earth', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Pick', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Lament, and Visions of Hope, for Wronged Souls', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Skinfolk: An American Show (Play)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walker, Jillian (Playwright)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bushwick Starr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Black Theater', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-06T23:33:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jose Solís', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jose', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Solís', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c99c39a7-af06-515d-9fb1-a4187b0f3ba8', 'word_count': 579, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c99c39a7-af06-515d-9fb1-a4187b0f3ba8'}, {'abstract': 'The less quantifiable elements of Mr. Biden’s campaign — including his association with Barack Obama, his empathy and his momentum — have outweighed his lack of organizational heft.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/06/us/politics/joe-biden-democratic-primary.html', 'snippet': 'The less quantifiable elements of Mr. Biden’s campaign — including his association with Barack Obama, his empathy and his momentum — have outweighed his lack of organizational heft.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Joseph R. Biden Jr.’s campaign organization in key Super Tuesday states was so flimsy that it shocked and alarmed Democratic Party leaders. Mr. Biden had little cash for advertising on the airwaves. His message just days before the big vote was sometimes unfocused and meandering.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/06/us/politics/06biden1/06biden1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/06/us/politics/06biden1/06biden1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/06/us/politics/06biden1/06biden1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/06/us/politics/06biden1/06biden1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/06/us/politics/06biden1/06biden1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/06/us/politics/06biden1/06biden1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thum