 retiring Republican congressman from North Carolina and one of President Trump’s most ardent defenders, becomes the latest chief of staff for a mercurial president who dispatched the previous three after they fell out of favor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/07/us/politics/mark-meadows-trump-chief-of-staff.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Meadows, a retiring Republican congressman from North Carolina and one of President Trump’s most ardent defenders, becomes the latest chief of staff for a mercurial president who dispatched the previous three after they fell out of favor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PALM BEACH, Fla. — One day last month, Mark Meadows went on Fox News to defend President Trump’s decision to begin purging the government of officials perceived to be disloyal to him. “Part of his administration is trying to defeat the Trump agenda,” Mr. Meadows declared.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/08/us/politics/07dc-meadows-print/merlin_169629144_c3e79ef1-aeab-4266-8d29-aa28bc0c807c-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/08/us/politics/07dc-meadows-print/merlin_169629144_c3e79ef1-aeab-4266-8d29-aa28bc0c807c-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/08/us/politics/07dc-meadows-print/merlin_169629144_c3e79ef1-aeab-4266-8d29-aa28bc0c807c-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/08/us/politics/07dc-meadows-print/merlin_169629144_c3e79ef1-aeab-4266-8d29-aa28bc0c807c-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': '