anizations', 'value': 'Boeing Company', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kenya', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indonesia', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lion Air', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-09T13:31:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Marks and Abdi Latif Dahir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Marks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Abdi', 'middlename': 'Latif', 'lastname': 'Dahir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d67d678d-0f3f-5d7b-9af2-ae0d44a75dc5', 'word_count': 1033, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d67d678d-0f3f-5d7b-9af2-ae0d44a75dc5'}, {'abstract': 'Your tickets for concerts and soccer games are useless. Your children can’t go to school. Even Mass is canceled.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/09/opinion/italy-coronavirus.html', 'snippet': 'Your tickets for concerts and soccer games are useless. Your children can’t go to school. Even Mass is canceled.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MILAN — You glance at the headlines, just before going to bed on a Saturday evening, to discover your town has been put in lockdown. Or is about to be. It’s not clear. Apparently, the order hasn’t been signed yet. Social media shows people rushing to the station, mainly for the last trains south. This is Milan, economic dynamo of Italy, the only city in the country that has grown stronger and richer through the long years of stagnation since the financial crisis of 2008. An enormous number of people who work here are from the south. If the city is shutting down for the coronavirus, they want to be home.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multi