 depiction of gay characters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mart Crowley, whose 1968 play, “The Boys in the Band,” put gay characters and their stories front and center in a way that had rarely been seen in a mainstream New York theater, died on Saturday night in Manhattan. He was 84.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/10/obituaries/06crowley2-print/merlin_137417328_a13e9648-cd3e-4485-bd2f-6f84dde32515-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/10/obituaries/06crowley2-print/merlin_137417328_a13e9648-cd3e-4485-bd2f-6f84dde32515-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/10/obituaries/06crowley2-print/merlin_137417328_a13e9648-cd3e-4485-bd2f-6f84dde32515-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/10/obituaries/06crowley2-print/merlin_137417328_a13e9648-cd3e-4485-bd2f-6f84dde32515-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/10/obituaries/06crowley2-print/06crowley2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/10/obituaries/06crowley2-print/06crowley2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/10/obituaries/06crowley2-print/06crowley2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mart Crowley, ‘Boys in the Band’ Playwright, Dies at 84', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mart Crowley, 84, Dies; Broke Ground by Writing Gay Themes in His Plays', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crowley, Mart', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality and Bisexuality', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Boys in the Band (Play)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-09T15:55:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Obits', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0ffb9ba-ba84-53de-a57b-9dc5b1828fe2', 'word_count': 975, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0ffb9ba-ba84-53de-a57b-9dc5b1828fe2'}, {'abstract': 'Playing with Coltrane and leading his own groups, the pianist’s indelible style stood on its own.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/09/arts/music/mccoy-tyner-essential-recordings.html', 'snippet': 'Playing with Coltrane and leading his own groups, the pianist’s indelible style stood on its own.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The pianist McCoy Tyner’s impact on music is usually explained through his relationship to John Coltrane, a childhood friend who became his boss in one of the most significant ensembles in American history. But the story of Mr. Tyner, who died on Friday, is also the story of a bandleader and composer whose granite style remained intact even as he tracked