': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/10/multimedia/09-Parenting-takekidtoplayground/09-Parenting-takekidtoplayground-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/10/multimedia/09-Parenting-takekidtoplayground/09-Parenting-takekidtoplayground-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/10/multimedia/09-Parenting-takekidtoplayground/09-Parenting-takekidtoplayground-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '11 Questions Parents May Have About Coronavirus', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Be Cautious, but Not Panicked, About Your Children', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hygiene and Cleanliness', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-09T20:25:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Parenting', 'section_name': 'Parenting', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jessica Grose', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grose', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c892bb1e-64dd-5e87-86b0-2a60e253221f', 'word_count': 1998, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c892bb1e-64dd-5e87-86b0-2a60e253221f'}, {'abstract': 'Monday night is fried chicken night at the TAK Room, where the chef is serving his Ad Hoc dish.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/09/dining/thomas-keller-fried-chicken.html', 'snippet': 'Monday night is fried chicken night at the TAK Room, where the chef is serving his Ad Hoc dish.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The chef Thomas Keller’s talent for frying chicken is such that many years ago he opened a family-style restaurant, Ad Hoc, down the road from his French Laundry in Yountville, Calif., where it was and still is the specialty. Now it’s landing in New York, at his elegant TAK Room in Hudson Yards, on Monday nights starting next week. He said that it was in response to popular demand and that he saw it as a way to play down the restaurant’s luxe feel. It will also be served on Monday evenings starting next week at another one of his places, The Surf Club Restaurant, in Surfside, Fla. A gluten-free version is available. The chicken comes with a couple of sides, often lush macaroni and cheese, delectable collard greens or feathery buttermilk biscuits. It’s not sold to go, but you can always order enough for leftovers to take home.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/11/dining/09Burner-fry/09Burner-fry-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/11/dining/09Burner-fry/09Burner-fry-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/11/dining/09Burner-fry/09Burner-fry-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/11/dining/09Burner-fry/09Burner-fry-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1355, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/11/dining/09Burner-fry/09Burner-fry-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/11/dining/09Burner-fry/09Burner-fry-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/11/dining/09Burner-fry/09Burner-fry-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chicken, the Thomas Keller Way', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Savor: Monday Night Is for Fried Chicken', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poultry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TAK Room (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keller, Thomas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-09T20:32:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7a639fb-ba76-53b5-b0b0-505304b08f6f', 'word_count': 195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7a639fb-ba76-53b5-b0b0-505304b08f6f'}, {'abstract': 'As state housing commissioner, he pushed a law that let landlords charge market rates when apartments became vacant. He also shepherded Battery Park City.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/09/nyregion/charles-urstadt-dead.html', 'snippet': 'As state housing commissioner, he pushed a law that let landlords charge market rates when apartments became vacant. He also shepherded Battery Park City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Charles J. Urstadt, a major influence in New York State housing who helped ease rent controls and laid the groundwork for the construction of Battery Park City in Lower Manhattan, died on March 3 at his home in Bronxville, N.Y. He was 91.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/10/obituaries/09Urstadt-print/merlin_20318715_d573d4ec-012f-48b7-a849-77b13885a877-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/10/obituaries/09Urstadt-print/merlin_20318715_d573d4ec-012f-48b7-a849-77b13885a877-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/10/obituaries/09Urstadt-print/merlin_20318715_d573d4ec-012f-48b7-a849-77b13885a877-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/10/obituaries/09Urstadt-print/merlin_20318715_d573d4ec-012f-48b7-a849-77b13885a877-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/10/obituaries/09Urstadt-print/09Urstadt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/10/obituaries/09Urstadt-print/09Urstadt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/10/obituaries/09Urstadt-print/09Urstadt-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Charles Urstadt, Who Eased N.Y. Rent Controls, Dies at 91', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Charles Urstadt, 91, Force in Real Estate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rent Control and Stabilization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Battery Park City Authority', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Empire State Development Corp', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Urstadt, Charles J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Battery Park City (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-09T20:36:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Obits', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/f421a949-f782-5181-8755-88db0f881b4e', 'word_count': 828, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f421a949-f782-5181-8755-88db0f881b4e'}, {'abstract': 'The Brooklyn Cider House hosts a fermentation festival with pickles, kombucha, sake and, yes, cider.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/09/dining/fermentation-festival-brooklyn.html', 'snippet': 'The Brooklyn Cider House hosts a fermentation festival with pickles, kombucha, sake and, yes, cider.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You can get your fizz and pucker on at the city’s first fermentation festival, a gathering of foods and drinks that rely on the chemistry of yeasts, molds and bacteria. More than 20 local companies will be on hand with pickles, kombucha, beer, cheese, bread, wine, sake, cured meats, kimchi and, since it’s organized by Brooklyn Cider House, ciders. Products can be sampled and bought.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/11/dining/09Burner-Fizz/merlin_170226702_f5185017-653b-4d9f-a4db-831ebdffbd59-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/11/dining/09Burner-Fizz/merlin_170226702_f5185017-653b-4d9f-a4db-831ebdffbd59-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/11/dining/09Burner-Fizz/merlin_170226702_f5185017-653b-4d9f-a4db-831ebdffbd59-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/11/dining/09Burner-Fizz/merlin_170226702_f5185017-653b-4d9f-a4db-831ebdffbd59-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/11/dining/09Burner-Fizz/merlin_170226702_f5185017-653b-4d9f-a4db-831ebdffbd59-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/11/dining/09Burner-Fizz/merlin_170226702_f5185017-653b-4d9f-a4db-831ebdffbd59-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/11/dining/09Burner-Fizz/merlin_170226702_f5185017-653b-4d9f-a4db-831ebdffbd59-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'This Festival Brings the Funk', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Sample: Fermentation Festival  Brings the Funk', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Cider House (Brooklyn, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-09T20:39:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d44d267c-9633-5e67-bc78-b78e79d89c54', 'word_count': 129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d44d267c-9633-5e67-bc78-b78e79d89c54'}, {'abstract': 'A new vegan deli product mimics the flavor of the Reuben staple.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/09/dining/vegan-meat-corned-beef.html', 'snippet': 'A new vegan deli product mimics the flavor of the Reuben staple.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s a new player on the mock-meat front: vegan corned beef. Jenny Goldfarb, a vegan for nearly 10 years whose family was in the Jewish deli business in New York, decided that the taste of a hefty corned beef sandwich or a Reuben should not be on vegans’ no-fly list. She spent months in her kitchen experimenting with wheat, chickpeas, beets, tomatoes, spices, sweeteners and yeast, and finally, in 2018, began introducing the results in Los Angeles. Sarge’s Delicatessen & Diner in New York started serving her Mrs. Goldfarb’s Unreal Deli Corned Beef in January. It’s increasingly sold nationwide. The “meat” approximates the slightly crumbly texture of the real thing fairly well, and delivers its salty, somewhat smoky flavor. (It’s also kosher.) It’s a true departure from the usual burgers and sausages that vegan meat mimics. But what’s missing is the fat, especially for those, like me, who do not prefer lean corned beef. Thus, it’s best in a sandwich dressed with mustard and coleslaw or in a Reuben, in the company of gooey Russian dressing, melting vegan cheese and a moist layer of sauerkraut.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/11/dining/09Burner-beef/merlin_169959837_d7b1a314-9849-4d13-b4e0-120109257c49-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/11/dining/09Burner-beef/merlin_169959837_d7b1a314-9849-4d13-b4e0-120109257c49-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/11/dining/09Burner-beef/merlin_169959837_d7b1a314-9849-4d13-b4e0-120109257c49-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/11/dining/09Burner-beef/merlin_169959837_d7b1a314-9849-4d13-b4e0-120109257c49-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/11/dining/09Burner-beef/merlin_169959837_d7b1a314-9849-4d13-b4e0-120109257c49-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/11/dining/09Burner-beef/merlin_169959837_d7b1a314-9849-4d13-b4e0-120109257c49-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/11/dining/09Burner-beef/merlin_169959837_d7b1a314-9849-4d13-b4e0-120109257c49-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Corned Beef, Hold the Beef', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Amaze: Corned Beef, Minus the Beef', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veganism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Delicatessens', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-09T20:43:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7253da26-e003-5aa9-8cdb-22431832f5c0', 'word_count': 225, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7253da26-e003-5aa9-8cdb-22431832f5c0'}, {'abstract': 'Should you wear a mask? Does airplane travel pose a greater risk? Do hand sanitizers work? Health professionals offer some tips.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/09/travel/coronavirus-travel-sick.html', 'snippet': 'Should you wear a mask? Does airplane travel pose a greater risk? Do hand sanitizers work? Health professionals offer some tips.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wary travelers are donning masks on New York City subways and in San Francisco airports. Panicked consumers are arming themselves with disinfectants. Businesses are suspending operations and airlines are halting flights.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 