game over who is politicizing the coronavirus.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/10/us/politics/wuhan-virus.html', 'snippet': 'Despite the recommendations of health officials, some conservatives are using the term to describe Covid-19, prompting a blame game over who is politicizing the coronavirus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The name Covid-19 was clinical and nondescript, and that was exactly the point when the World Health Organization revealed it to guard against stigmatization of the place from which it originated. But a month later, the recommended terminology for the coronavirus has not extended to every corner of politics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/09/us/politics/09dc-virustalk-1/merlin_169720776_c5388f13-c3c0-441c-95ac-e74d0dc1b7e3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/09/us/politics/09dc-virustalk-1/merlin_169720776_c5388f13-c3c0-441c-95ac-e74d0dc1b7e3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/09/us/politics/09dc-virustalk-1/merlin_169720776_c5388f13-c3c0-441c-95ac-e74d0dc1b7e3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/09/us/politics/09dc-virustalk-1/merlin_169720776_c5388f13-c3c0-441c-95ac-e74d0dc1b7e3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/09/us/politics/09dc-virustalk-1/merlin_169720776_c5388f13-c3c0-441c-95ac-e74d0dc1b7e3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'he