ank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kudlow, Lawrence A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mnuchin, Steven T', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Navarro, Peter', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-10T14:48:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Tankersley and Alan Rappeport', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tankersley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rappeport', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7197b6d-43a3-5f67-9e80-20657a29896a', 'word_count': 903, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7197b6d-43a3-5f67-9e80-20657a29896a'}, {'abstract': 'Home-cooked lunches and no commuting while we deal with coronavirus can’t compensate for what’s lost in creativity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/10/technology/working-from-home.html', 'snippet': 'Home-cooked lunches and no commuting while we deal with coronavirus can’t compensate for what’s lost in creativity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m writing this from the makeshift quarantine bunker in my dining room — sweatpants on, hand sanitizer nearby, snacking my way through my emergency rations. I’m getting plenty of work done, but I’m starting to get unnerved by the lack of stimulation. It’s been hours (days?) since I interacted face to face with a human who is not related to me, and cabin fever is setting in.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sorry, but Working From Home Is Overrated', 'kicker': 'The Shift', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Work From Home? Think Again', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telecommuting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Work-Life Balance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Productivity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Workplace Environment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Videophones and Videoconferencing', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-10T14:53:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin Roose', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roose', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37834ada-33f0-5f20-844d-e2beeeaccf86', 'word_count': 1107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37834ada-33f0-5f20-844d-e2beeeaccf86'}, {'abstract': 'Zenith’s El Primero was once considered a mechanical marvel. Now, it’s achieved cult classic status.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/10/t-magazine/zenith-el-primero-watch.html', 'snippet': 'Zenith’s El Primero was once considered a mechanical marvel. Now, it’s achieved cult classic status.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The world’s first high-frequency automatic chronograph was introduced in 1969 by Zenith, a Swiss watchmaker founded more than a century before in the town of Le Locle. Unrivaled in timing precision (to one-tenth of a second) with a barrel-shaped tonneau case displaying a round dial with three charcoal-tinted subdials, the El Primero was considered a mechanical marvel; its chronograph module used an entirely integrated caliber, not just one bolted to an existing automatic movement. But the El Primero wasn’t on top for long: Just a few years later, quartz — an element that enabled watches to tell time even more accurately — threatened to make mechanical watches obsolete. Luckily, Zenith’s chronograph, along with the company, was saved when, in 1988, Rolex used the elegantly slender, self-winding caliber to power an updated version of its classic Daytona, which turned the movement into a cult favorite. Fifty years after El Primero’s debut, the company has released a timepiece that pays homage to the original 1969 model. Just two small tweaks were needed to bring it into the present: The hollow links of the original bracelet designed by the renowned Geneva firm Gay Frères have been rendered in solid steel; and there’s now a sapphire crystal caseback, the better to fixate endlessly on a timepiece that helped fine horology take a leap into the future. $8,200, zenith-watches.com.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/10/t-magazine/10tmag-anotherthing/10tmag-anotherthing-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/10/t-magazine/10tmag-anotherthing/10tmag-anotherthing-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/10/t-magazine/10tmag-anotherthing/10tmag-anotherthing-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 769, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/10/t-magazine/10tmag-anotherthing/10tmag-anotherthing-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1537, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/10/t-magazine/10tmag-anotherthing/10tmag-anotherthing-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/10/t-magazine/10tmag-anotherthing/10tmag-anotherthing-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/10/t-magazine/10tmag-anotherthing/10tmag-anotherthing-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Watch Brought Back From the Brink of Extinction', 'kicker': 'Another Thing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Watches and Clocks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rolex SA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zenith SA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Switzerland', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-10T15:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nancy Hass', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nancy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hass', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b28abf9-5aeb-5718-a5e6-b5a2a63caecb', 'word_count': 227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b28abf9-5aeb-5718-a5e6-b5a2a63caecb'}, {'abstract': 'It’s tricky to pack our small spaces with supplies, but the real struggle is deciding how worried to be.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/10/opinion/coronavirus-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'It’s tricky to pack our small spaces with supplies, but the real struggle is deciding how worried to be.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Because my apartment is too small to store the recommended pandemic preparedness supplies without turning the space into an obstacle course, the packages of water, peanut butter, canned soup, granola bars, pasta, tomato sauce, Theraflu, DayQuil, and Purell now protrude from under my girlfriend’s dining room table (which is also the kitchen table and living room table) in her slightly bigger place, where I spend half of my weeknights anyway.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/10/opinion/10TalmonSmith/merlin_170115795_4d56b1b2-b642-48f5-afad-56c6a16f2d90-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/10/opinion/10TalmonSmith/merlin_170115795_4d56b1b2-b642-48f5-afad-56c6a16f2d90-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/10/opinion/10TalmonSmith/merlin_170115795_4d56b1b2-b642-48f5-afad-56c6a16f2d90-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 686, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/10/opinion/10TalmonSmith/merlin_170115795_4d56b1b2-b642-48f5-afad-56c6a16f2d90-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1371, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/10/opinion/10TalmonSmith/10TalmonSmith-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/10/opinion/10TalmonSmith/10TalmonSmith-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/10/opinion/10TalmonSmith/10TalmonSmith-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Halfhearted Millennial Coronavirus Prep in a New York City Apartment', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-10T15:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Talmon Joseph Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Talmon', 'middlename': 'Joseph', 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/777632b7-edc3-5979-b5a7-28021cb836e2', 'word_count': 958, 'uri': 'nyt://article/777632b7-edc3-5979-b5a7-28021cb836e2'}, {'abstract': 'With the deaths of 18 residents in a single nursing home amid a coronavirus outbreak in Washington State, industry leaders recommend strict limits on visits at nursing homes across the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/10/us/coronavirus-nursing-homes-washington-seattle.html', 'snippet': 'With the deaths of 18 residents in a single nursing home amid a coronavirus outbreak in Washington State, industry leaders recommend strict limits on visits at nursing homes across the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'STANWOOD, Wash. — At nursing homes where guests are barred because of the coronavirus, adult children talk to their parents through locked glass doors like jailhouse visitors. They worry it may be months before they can hug each other again. Many families are debating whether to move their frail loved ones out altogether and care for them at home.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/10/us/10VIRUS-NURSING-kirkland-window/10VIRUS-NURSING-kirkland-window-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 447, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/10/us/10VIRUS-NURSING-kirkland-window/10VIRUS-NURSING-kirkland-window-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 447}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/10/us/10VIRUS-NURSING-kirkland-window/10VIRUS-NURSING-kirkland-window-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 762, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/10/us/10VIRUS-NURSING-kirkland-window/10VIRUS-NURSING-kirkland-window-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1524, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/10/us/10VIRUS-NURSING-kirkland-window/10VIRUS-NURSING-kirkland-window-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/10/us/10VIRUS-NURSING-kirkland-window/10VIRUS-NURSING-kirkland-window-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/10/us/10VIRUS-NURSING-kirkland-window/10VIRUS-NURSING-kirkland-window-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thu