31c006d7-69c8-5088-8918-f55bf7919dfc'}, {'abstract': 'As the coronavirus spreads, the public interest demands that employers abandon their longstanding resistance to paid sick leave.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/11/opinion/coronavirus-paid-sick-leave.html', 'snippet': 'As the coronavirus spreads, the public interest demands that employers abandon their longstanding resistance to paid sick leave.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Walmart, the nation’s largest private employer, set a standard for the rest of the private sector on Tuesday by announcing that, in addition to its existing paid sick leave policy, it would provide up to two weeks of paid leave for employees who fall ill or are quarantined because of a confirmed exposure to the coronavirus.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/11/opinion/11sickpaidleave_sub/11sickpaidleave_sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/11/opinion/11sickpaidleave_sub/11sickpaidleave_sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/11/opinion/11sickpaidleave_sub/11sickpaidleave_sub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/11/opinion/11sickpaidleave_sub/11sickpaidleave_sub-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/11/opinion/11sickpaidleave_sub/11sickpaidleave_sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbS