ps://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/11/movies/bloodshot-review.html', 'snippet': 'Vin Diesel brings the right balance of contemplativeness and meatheadedness to this action film.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ray Garrison, Vin Diesel’s character in “Bloodshot,” could be a distant relative of the Terminators. A dead soldier returned to life, Ray has a new bloodstream made up of “nanites,” insectlike robots that quickly heal his wounds. He can punch through concrete. He can have his face blown apart and keep shooting while it reassembles. He is — this may not be the technical term — Wi-Fi-enabled, meaning he can instantly download and digest a piloting manual, just like in “The Matrix.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/13/arts/bloodshot1/bloodshot1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 463, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/13/arts/bloodshot1/bloodshot1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 463}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/13/arts/bloodshot1/bloodshot1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 790, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/13/arts/bloodshot1/bloodshot1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1580, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/13/arts/bloodshot1/bloodshot1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/13/arts/bloodshot1/bloodshot1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'r