cle', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Kenigsberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kenigsberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/31a435fb-99eb-5a4a-a37b-a267b222d5a5', 'word_count': 310, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31a435fb-99eb-5a4a-a37b-a267b222d5a5'}, {'abstract': 'Adam Bolt’s new documentary focuses on Crispr technology, which can edit genes, thus giving people the ability to change human, animal and plant life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/12/movies/human-nature-review.html', 'snippet': 'Adam Bolt’s new documentary focuses on Crispr technology, which can edit genes, thus giving people the ability to change human, animal and plant life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every “Oh wow” in “Human Nature” is matched by an “Oh no” somewhere down the line. Together, these two competing emotions — excitement and unease — make for one pretty fascinating documentary.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/12/arts/12humannature-art/12humannature-art-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/12/arts/12humannature-art/12humannature-art-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/12/arts/12humannature-art/12humannature-art-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/12/arts/12humannature-art/12humannature-art-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/12/arts/12humannature-art/12humannature-art-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/12/arts/12humannature-art/12humannature-art-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/12/arts/12humannature-art/12humannature-art-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Human Nature’ Review: We Can Now Alter Our DNA. But Should We?', 'kicker': 'critic’s pick', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Change By a Snip Of DNA', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crispr (DNA)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Human Nature (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bolt, Adam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-12T11:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Jaworowski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jaworowski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/49477f1e-c24c-52b4-abdc-a1635c5e4f3c', 'word_count': 302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49477f1e-c24c-52b4-abdc-a1635c5e4f3c'}, {'abstract': 'A high school student comes of age under the misguidance of his stoner B.F.F. in this comedy by Jason Orley.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/12/movies/big-time-adolescence-review.html', 'snippet': 'A high school student comes of age under the misguidance of his stoner B.F.F. in this comedy by Jason Orley.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pete Davidson, the “Saturday Night Live” bad boy, is a natural at playing the guy your parents want you to stay away from. His character in “Big Time Adolescence,” the tatted, platinum-haired, foul-mouthed Zeke, feels like an extension of the Davidson we see in the tabloids. A 23-year-old slacker who never grew up, Zeke spends his time smoking weed and being a bad influence on his fawning minion, the 16-year-old Mo (Griffin Gluck), his ex-girlfriend’s younger brother.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/12/arts/12BIGTIMEPIX/12BIGTIMEPIX-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/12/arts/12BIGTIMEPIX/12BIGTIMEPIX-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/12/arts/12BIGTIMEPIX/12BIGTIMEPIX-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/12/arts/12BIGTIMEPIX/12BIGTIMEPIX-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/12/arts/12BIGTIMEPIX/12BIGTIMEPIX-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/12/arts/12BIGTIMEPIX/12BIGTIMEPIX-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/12/arts/12BIGTIMEPIX/12BIGTIMEPIX-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Big Time Adolescence’ Review: Pete Davidson as Role Model', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Big Time  Adolescence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davidson, Pete (1993- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Big Time Adolescence (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Orley, Jason', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-12T11:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kristen Yoonsoo Kim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kristen', 'middlename': 'Yoonsoo', 'lastname': 'Kim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/50f62962-59a5-59d7-953d-10ca3578c303', 'word_count': 271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50f62962-59a5-59d7-953d-10ca3578c303'}, {'abstract': 'Sally Potter’s new film stars Javier Bardem as a man tormented by visions of his other potential lives. But there’s little lightness negotiating with the dark.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/12/movies/roads-not-taken-review.html', 'snippet': 'Sally Potter’s new film stars Javier Bardem as a man tormented by visions of his other potential lives. But there’s little lightness negotiating with the dark.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Right off the bat, a new movie written and directed by Sally Potter does not take it easy on the viewer. It opens with plain white-on-black titles followed by the sight of Javier Bardem in a bed, in a barely furnished apartment. He lies alone, staring at the ceiling, grunting and mumbling. His guttural utterances are sometimes more frightening than pitiful.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/12/arts/12theroads-art/merlin_170127726_aedfcbf6-84c1-48ba-9896-54a2fdaaa2ba-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 448, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/12/arts/12theroads-art/merlin_170127726_aedfcbf6-84c1-48ba-9896-54a2fdaaa2ba-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 448}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/12/arts/12theroads-art/merlin_170127726_aedfcbf6-84c1-48ba-9896-54a2fdaaa2ba-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 764, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/12/arts/12theroads-art/merlin_170127726_aedfcbf6-84c1-48ba-9896-54a2fdaaa2ba-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1529, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/12/arts/12theroads-art/12theroads-art-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/12/arts/12theroads-art/12theroads-art-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/12/arts/12theroads-art/12theroads-art-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Roads Not