ww.nytimes.com/2020/03/12/arts/music/francis-and-the-lights.html', 'snippet': 'Three days in the creative wilderness with Francis Farewell Starlite, the reclusive muse to Kanye West, Bon Iver and Drake.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEBASTOPOL, Calif. — On the morning of Dec. 1 last year, the musician Francis Farewell Starlite posted an announcement to his nearly 28,000 followers on Twitter. The message wasn’t an apology, per se, but its pointed brevity and dispassion conveyed a certain amount of heartache and embarrassment.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/15/arts/15francis1/merlin_166941957_a71a6f4b-72cd-4d4b-a3f6-d9d9716ae45c-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 840, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/15/arts/15francis1/merlin_166941957_a71a6f4b-72cd-4d4b-a3f6-d9d9716ae45c-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 840}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/15/arts/15francis1/merlin_166941957_a71a6f4b-72cd-4d4b-a3f6-d9d9716ae45c-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 732, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/15/arts/15francis1/merlin_166941957_a71a6f4b-72cd-4d4b-a3f6-d9d9716ae45c-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1463, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/15/arts/15francis1/15francis1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/15/arts/15francis1/15francis1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/15/arts/15francis1/15francis1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Francis and the Lights, Pop Star Interrupted', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Musician Feeling Lost Rethinks His Path', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pop and Rock Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Francis and the Lights', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Starlite, Francis Farewell', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-12T14:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Reggie Ugwu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Reggie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ugwu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a3cfaba-3a7e-5c0a-bddc-9b7841da85f1', 'word_count': 2572, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a3cfaba-3a7e-5c0a-bddc-9b7841da85f1'}, {'abstract': 'If you’ve done a musical in Marin County, you know the name Marilyn Izdebski, who has directed more than 10,000 kids over 41 years. Many cities have someone like her.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/12/theater/beyond-broadway-stacy-wolf.html', 'snippet': 'If you’ve done a musical in Marin County, you know the name Marilyn Izdebski, who has directed more than 10,000 kids over 41 years. Many cities have someone like her.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN ANSELMO, Calif. — When I arrive at the theater — a barnlike building on the leafy campus of the San Francisco Theological Seminary — to watch the dress rehearsal for “42nd Street,” a petite, bright-eyed woman in her mid-60s warmly greets me. She has perfect posture; her dark hair is in a bun with a pencil stuck through it, and a pair of reading glasses hangs around her neck. She wears black yoga pants, a black zip-up sweater, a black scarf around her neck, white athletic socks and black clogs. This is Marilyn Izdebski’s uniform.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/15/arts/15beyond-excerpt-1/merlin_169861113_ff0de5f8-1b59-4f9a-946f-8aa1e67c078c-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/15/arts/15beyond-excerpt-1/merlin_169861113_ff0de5f8-1b59-4f9a-946f-8aa1e67c078c-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 480}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/15/arts/15beyond-excerpt-1/merlin_169861113_ff0de5f8-1b59-4f9a-946f-8aa1e67c078c-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/15/arts/15beyond-excerpt-1/merlin_169861113_ff0de5f8-1b59-4f9a-946f-8aa1e67c078c-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1638, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/15/arts/15beyond-excerpt-1/15beyond-excerpt-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/15/arts/15beyond-excerpt-1/15beyond-excerpt-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/15/arts/15beyond-excerpt-1/15beyond-excerpt-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Out of the Spotlight, Still a Star: The ‘Backstage Diva’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Out of the Spotlight, Still a Star', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Izdebski, Marilyn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Beyond Broadway: The Pleasure and Promise of Musical Theatre Across America (Book)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-12T14:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stacy Wolf', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stacy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wolf', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5252eb30-785c-5cd7-9269-06f2d4296900', 'word_count': 1435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5252eb30-785c-5cd7-9269-06f2d4296900'}, {'abstract': 'In an unusual year with two titles, the studio stumbled a bit with “Onward.” But the clip for its next film, due in June, has a lot going for it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/12/movies/soul-pixar-jamie-foxx.html', 'snippet': 'In an unusual year with two titles, the studio stumbled a bit with “Onward.” But the clip for its next film, due in June, has a lot going for it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With a $39.1 million domestic opening, Pixar’s “Onward” was considered a box-office disappointment last weekend, at least by the animation label’s elevated standards. Disney usually puts out only one Pixar film a year, but that’s not the plan for 2020. “Soul” is slated to come out in June, and the studio just released the film’s first full trailer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank'