9. But hoarding unnecessary items can deplete the supply for everyone else.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tweets and videos of people panic-buying toilet paper are proliferating on social media. Yes, being prepared for a possible quarantine is smart. But the above video explains why overbuying certain items is not. An excess of toilet paper will not help protect you against Covid-19, but it will cause a run on supplies that keeps others from getting what they might need.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/12/opinion/op-panic-buying/op-panic-buying-articleLarge.png', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/12/opinion/op-panic-buying/op-panic-buying-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/12/opinion/op-panic-buying/op-panic-buying-jumbo.png', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/12/opinion/op-panic-buying/op-panic-buying-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1080, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/12/opinion/op-panic-buying/op-panic-buying-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/12/opinion/op-panic-buying/op-panic-buying-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/12/opinion/op-panic-buying/op-panic-buying-thumbLarge.png', 'height