: 'Carey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2430d60d-400f-5d30-9ffe-0b54e3fd89d7', 'word_count': 1419, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2430d60d-400f-5d30-9ffe-0b54e3fd89d7'}, {'abstract': 'The chef and stylist Gina Correll Aglietti, a co-founder of Yola Mezcal, shares her tips for hosting a casual backyard meal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/13/t-magazine/gina-correll-aglietti-yola-mezcal.html', 'snippet': 'The chef and stylist Gina Correll Aglietti, a co-founder of Yola Mezcal, shares her tips for hosting a casual backyard meal.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I fell madly in love with Mexico City,” says the Los Angeles-based chef and stylist Gina Correll Aglietti of the 2010 trip on which she met one of her business partners, Yola Jimenez. “We had one of those really long Contramar lunches, like four hours,” says Jimenez, referring to a meal they shared at the acclaimed seafood restaurant after connecting through a mutual friend. It’s a summerlike evening in February at Aglietti’s home in Silver Lake, and Aglietti is sautéing fresh blue prawns in mezcal and chili oil while Jimenez leans against the kitchen counter, keeping her company. Later, at golden hour, just before sunset, guests will filter into the house — an R.M. Schindler-designed residence, built in 1934, with a floating, gabled roof and custom-built furniture — to celebrate the musician Danielle Haim’s 31st birthday. “Danielle loves seafood,” explains Aglietti, who is also planning to prepare red rock cod à la plancha.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/11/t-magazine/food/Agiletti-slide-BQVA/Agiletti-slide-BQVA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 720, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlar