a Do-Over', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Masters Postponement Leaves Hope for a Do-Over', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Masters Golf Tournament', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-13T14:25:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Pennington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pennington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ee8c270-0d40-579e-a907-31db149537fa', 'word_count': 906, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ee8c270-0d40-579e-a907-31db149537fa'}, {'abstract': 'Tejal Rao, our California restaurant critic and part of the Indian diaspora, has put together a rich portrait of the country’s home cooking.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/13/dining/the-essential-indian-recipes.html', 'snippet': 'Tejal Rao, our California restaurant critic and part of the Indian diaspora, has put together a rich portrait of the country’s home cooking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning. How are you doing? These are unsettling, anxiety-producing times, all over the world. We’re worried — about those we love and about ourselves, about the economy and politics and health of our nation and the ones at and beyond our borders. We’re freaked out about the person shuffling in line at the bank, by her dry cough and damp forehead, not to mention what we make of that character in vinyl gloves and a gas mask at the bagel store. (He’s not robbing the place, but calmly ordering a pound of blueberry cream cheese to take home to quarantine!) I myself bought four pounds of dried black beans at the market, 10 cans of tomato soup for $10, a sleeve of Irish Spring, a lot of bacon and butter and flour, frozen fruit, rice, two boxes of Red Zinger, shelf-stable milk. I don’t know what’s going on with me. You may feel similarly.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/11/dining/09Indianrex2-copy/merlin_169212648_9575b8e9-ce0d-471e-bead-9283b7197dc4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/11/dining/09Indianrex2-copy/merlin_169212648_9575b8e9-ce0d-471e-bead-9283b7197dc4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/11/dining/09Indianrex2-copy/merlin_169212648_9575b8e9-ce0d-471e-bead-9283b7197dc4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/11/dining/09Indianrex2-copy/merlin_169212648_9575b8e9-ce0d-471e-bead-9283b7197dc4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/11/dining/09Indianrex2-copy/09Indianrex2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/11/dining/09Indianrex2-copy/09Indianrex2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/11/dining/09Indianrex2-copy/09Indianrex2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Essential Indian Recipes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': No