the government’s powers in an extraordinary time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s well beyond the space limitations of this newsletter to summarize the new coronavirus developments of the last week internationally, let alone in Canada. Here at The Times, we’ve been drawing on our journalists around the world to produce a steady flow of reporting on the health crisis.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/13/world/13canadaletter-trudeau/merlin_170471670_3439ee68-a212-4aa7-ba72-2427151f7371-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/13/world/13canadaletter-trudeau/merlin_170471670_3439ee68-a212-4aa7-ba72-2427151f7371-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/13/world/13canadaletter-trudeau/merlin_170471670_3439ee68-a212-4aa7-ba72-2427151f7371-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/13/world/13canadaletter-trudeau/merlin_170471670_3439ee68-a212-4aa7-ba72-2427151f7371-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/13/world/13canadaletter-trudeau/13canadaletter-trudeau-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/13/world/13canadaletter-trudeau/13canadaletter-trudeau-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/13/world/13canadaletter-trudeau/13canadaletter-trudeau-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Far Can Canada Go to Slow Spread of the New Coronavirus?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-13T22:25:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Canada', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8df964a-437a-5a96-b54b-511cc5ccee72', 'word_count': 1051, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8df964a-437a-5a96-b54b-511cc5ccee72'}, {'abstract': 'He supported George Wallace’s 1968 presidential bid. But after a change of heart, he worked for civil rights and other progressive causes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/13/us/politics/tom-turnipseed-dead.html', 'snippet': 'He supported George Wallace’s 1968 presidential bid. But after a change of heart, he worked for civil rights and other progressive causes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tom Turnipseed, who after working on the presidential campaign of the segregationist George C. Wallace in 1968 took a 180-degree turn and became a prominent champion of civil rights, died on March 6 at his home in Columbia, S.C. He was 83.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'sub