n all of us whereby we often consider the situation we’re in to be especially dire, compared to others, even when we switch positions in the struggle of life.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Variety: Acrostic', 'kicker': 'SUNDAY VARIETY COLUMN', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2020-03-14T15:40:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Games', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Caitlin Lovinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Caitlin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd1d69d7-b40c-5ea1-9905-d34f3c6a1f6a', 'word_count': 206, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd1d69d7-b40c-5ea1-9905-d34f3c6a1f6a'}, {'abstract': 'As the coronavirus spreads, the public interest requires employers to abandon their longstanding resistance to paid sick leave.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/14/opinion/sunday/coronavirus-paid-sick-leave.html', 'snippet': 'As the coronavirus spreads, the public interest requires employers to abandon their longstanding resistance to paid sick leave.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most American restaurants do not offer paid sick leave. Workers who fall sick face a simple choice: Work and get paid or stay home and get stiffed. Not surprisingly, the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention reported in 2014 that fully 20 percent of food service workers had come to work at least once in the previous year “while sick with vomiting or diarrhea.”', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/14/opinion/14sickleave/14sickleave-articleLarge.png', 'height': 585, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'cro