care. Mr. Biden also committed to choosing a woman as a running mate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/15/us/politics/biden-sanders-debate-recap.html', 'snippet': 'With the coronavirus as a backdrop, and with no audience in attendance, the two Democrats were at times feisty discussing their differences over health care. Mr. Biden also committed to choosing a woman as a running mate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Joseph R. Biden Jr. and Senator Bernie Sanders called for vastly more aggressive government action to battle the coronavirus but split over some of the details along familiar ideological lines on Sunday night, as the two Democrats tangled over the right to lead their party into a campaign overshadowed by the pandemic inflicting havoc on the country’s economy and its social fabric.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Biden and Sanders Fight Over Policy and Records in Head-to-Head Debate', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two Rivals Take On Outbreak, and Each Other', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2020', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanders, Bernard', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-16T01:56:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexander Burns and Jonathan Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexander', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/586c9732-b9f7-5fcc-8b78-1adbe8056305', 'word_count': 1837, 'uri': 'nyt://article/586c9732-b9f7-5fcc-8b78-1adbe8056305'}, {'abstract': 'The new season brings the story, and a vengeful Dolores, outside the park, giving the series a needed jolt.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/15/arts/television/westworld-season-3-premiere-recap.html', 'snippet': 'The new season brings the story, and a vengeful Dolores, outside the park, giving the series a needed jolt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The opening sequence of the third season of “Westworld” naturally recalls the opening sequence of the first, when the wholesome rancher’s daughter Dolores Abernathy (Evan Rachel Wood) was still stuck in her loop, greeting beautiful days that typically ended in rape and murder. Now she remembers everything, including the 1 percenters who made her part of their bachelor weekends, and she’s finally in their world, leading an android vendetta that turns these people’s own technology against them. She can not only breach their security systems but also cue up a killer track from their Spotify playlists.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/15/arts/15westworld/merlin_170302041_9f3f1efc-b428-457a-909b-4d51f6eeb0e8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/15/arts/15westworld/merlin_170302041_9f3f1efc-b428-457a-909b-4d51f6eeb0e8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/15/arts/15westworld/merlin_170302041_9f3f1efc-b428-457a-909b-