us pandemic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/16/technology/france-apple-antitrust-fine.html', 'snippet': 'The fine comes as the iPhone maker deals with the impact of the coronavirus pandemic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — France’s antitrust regulator on Monday fined Apple 1.1 billion euros, or $1.2 billion, putting more pressure on the company as it grapples with the coronavirus outbreak that has threatened its supply chains and closed its retail stores.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/16/business/16apple/merlin_170511945_e3fafa5b-e68d-45c7-852b-7157bea6d097-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/16/business/16apple/merlin_170511945_e3fafa5b-e68d-45c7-852b-7157bea6d097-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/16/business/16apple/merlin_170511945_e3fafa5b-e68d-45c7-852b-7157bea6d097-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/16/business/16apple/merlin_170511945_e3fafa5b-e68d-45c7-852b-7157bea6d097-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/16/business/16apple/16apple-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/16/business/16apple/16apple-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/16/business/16apple/16apple-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'France Fines Apple $1.2 Billion for Antitrust Issues', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France Regulator Fines Apple $1.2 Billion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ingram Micro Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tech Data Corporation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-16T14:56:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David McCabe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McCabe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe9559e7-59d2-59d4-96e5-d5744825d23e', 'word_count': 448, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe9559e7-59d2-59d4-96e5-d5744825d23e'}, {'abstract': 'Cartier’s new Mauna necklace channels the combination of restraint and radiant excess brought to the house by the jewelry designer Jeanne Toussaint.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/16/t-magazine/cartier-mauna-necklace.html', 'snippet': 'Cartier’s new Mauna necklace channels the combination of restraint and radiant excess brought to the house by the jewelry designer Jeanne Toussaint.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the designer Jeanne Toussaint, known for both her lithe, turbaned elegance and her lasting friendship with Coco Chanel, was named by Louis Cartier as head of jewelry design at his family-run company in 1933, her restrained yet vibrant pieces came to define a new era of Art Deco abstraction. While later she became known for her realistic depictions of flowers and animals, especially the house’s now iconic panther (her nick\xadname was La Panthère), in the early years, she explored geometric form and unusual gems. Among them was the rare pinkish-orange imperial topaz, mined in the 19th century in western Russia’s Ural Mountains, when only the czar’s family were allowed to wear the stones. This new necklace features three exquisite imperial topazes from Brazil, including a dangling 11-carat pear-cut bicolor stone with an ombré effect that shifts from fuchsia to Tuscan yellow. Set off by diamonds, colored sapphires and rutilated quartz prized for its slash-like inclusions, it evokes Toussaint’s combustible combination of classical discipline and modern exuberance. Cartier Mauna necklace, price on request, (800) 227-8437.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/16/t-magazine/16tmag-thing/16tmag-thing-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/16/t-magazine/16tmag-thing/16tmag-thing-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/16/t-magazine/16tmag-thing/16tmag-thing-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumb