rams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c8bdd7f-3763-5a2d-a446-f32d1ad8020b', 'word_count': 1533, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c8bdd7f-3763-5a2d-a446-f32d1ad8020b'}, {'abstract': 'The threat of the virus, the school system’s most serious challenge in decades, means 1.1 million students need child care and other resources.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/16/nyregion/nyc-schools-closed-coronavirus.html', 'snippet': 'The threat of the virus, the school system’s most serious challenge in decades, means 1.1 million students need child care and other resources.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Adriana Cortés sat in a swing next to her 7-year-old daughter on Monday morning and watched her 10-year-old son kick a soccer ball against the fence. It would have been a blithe picture in the Sunnyside neighborhood of Queens, except for how the trio came to be there.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/16/nyregion/16nyvirus-schools1/merlin_170574699_223ec3db-35fb-4cf2-923a-32a98b319f9f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/16/nyregion/16nyvirus-schools1/merlin_170574699_223ec3db-35fb-4cf2-923a-32a98b319f9f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/16/nyregion/16nyvirus-schools1/merlin_170574699_223ec3db-35fb-4cf2-923a-32a98b319f9f-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/16/nyregion/16nyvirus-schools1/merlin_170574699_223ec3db-35fb-4cf2-923a-32a98b319f9f-superJ