: 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac8f8097-a8aa-5463-b736-948ce38306f5', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac8f8097-a8aa-5463-b736-948ce38306f5'}, {'abstract': 'For every known case of coronavirus, another five to 10 cases are out there undetected, a new study suggests.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/16/health/coronavirus-statistics-undetected.html', 'snippet': 'For every known case of coronavirus, another five to 10 cases are out there undetected, a new study suggests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scientists tracking the spread of the coronavirus reported on Monday that, for every confirmed case, there are most likely another five to 10 people in the community with undetected infections. These often-milder cases are, on average, about half as infectious as confirmed ones, but are responsible for nearly 80 percent of new cases, according to the report, which was based on data from China.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/16/science/16VIRUS-UNKNOWN/16VIRUS-UNKNOWN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/16/science/16VIRUS-UNKNOWN/16VIRUS-UNKNOWN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/16/science/16VIRUS-UNKNOWN/16VIRUS-UNKNOWN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/16/science/16VIRUS-UNKNOWN/16VIRUS-UNKNOWN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption