': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9a815e1-1d57-5cf0-92f5-9243407a05e3', 'word_count': 712, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9a815e1-1d57-5cf0-92f5-9243407a05e3'}, {'abstract': 'The companies funded Russia’s social media-fueled interference in the 2016 election, prosecutors said. But they tried to weaponize the case instead of fight it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/16/us/politics/concord-case-russian-interference.html', 'snippet': 'The companies funded Russia’s social media-fueled interference in the 2016 election, prosecutors said. But they tried to weaponize the case instead of fight it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Justice Department moved on Monday to drop charges against two Russian shell companies accused of financing schemes to interfere in the 2016 election, saying that they were exploiting the case to gain access to delicate information that Russia could weaponize.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/16/us/politics/16dc-justice/merlin_158373966_f62d4b80-9fe3-46f6-a0f6-90d0bcc7b5f5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/16/us/politics/16dc-justice/merlin_158373966_f62d4b80-9fe3-46f6-a0f6-90d0bcc7b5f5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/16/us/politics/16dc-justice/merlin_158373966_f62d4b80-9fe3-46f6-a0f6-90d0bcc7b5f5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/16/us/politics/16dc-justice/merlin_158373966_f62d4b80-9f