the touring industry are “preparing for the worst” as the coronavirus puts a halt to live shows.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/17/arts/music/concerts-cancelled-coronavirus.html', 'snippet': 'Sound engineers, lighting technicians and more gig-to-gig employees who fuel the touring industry are “preparing for the worst” as the coronavirus puts a halt to live shows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Joshua Dirks began last Thursday in Tulsa, Okla., as a lighting technician on Kiss’s arena tour. He ended the day on a bus home to Nashville as that tour — along with the rest of the multibillion-dollar concert industry — came to an abrupt halt.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/18/arts/17virus-touring2/merlin_170547372_ee6021dc-879c-4be8-9f4f-1c47a3b3b84d-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/18/arts/17virus-touring2/merlin_170547372_ee6021dc-879c-4be8-9f4f-1c47a3b3b84d-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/18/arts/17virus-touring2/merlin_170547372_ee6021dc-879c-4be8-9f4f-1c47a3b3b84d-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/18/arts/17virus-touring2/merlin_170547372_ee6021dc-879c-4be8-9f4f-1c47a3b3b84d-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/18/arts/17virus-touring2/17virus-touring2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/18/arts/17virus-touring2/17virus-touring2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/18/arts/17virus-touring2/17virus-touring2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Concerts Are on Hold. Workers Behind the Stars Are Hurting.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Headliner, No Audience, No Pay', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pop and Rock Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freelancing, Self-Employment and Independent Contracting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-17T09:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c419a70-413d-5f80-9f46-09e57bc4f554', 'word_count': 995, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c419a70-413d-5f80-9f46-09e57bc4f554'}, {'abstract': 'The call that upended Cynthiana, Ky., came around 5 p.m. on March 6. Officials had been bracing for the inevitable, and it had just arrived. A resident was sick. Five others would soon be, too.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/17/us/kentucky-coronavirus.html', 'snippet': 'The call that upended Cynthiana, Ky., came around 5 p.m. on March 6. Officials had been bracing for the inevitable, and it had just arrived. A resident was sick. Five others would soon be, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CYNTHIANA, Ky. — Closing in on a week after the coronavirus had descended on his small, rural community, James D. Smith sat behind a microphone in the WCYN studio on Main Street for his regular morning show, “Coffee Break Extra.” On his head, he wore a dark blue cap that said “mayor,” and in his eyes, the stress of the past several days.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/18/us/18VIRUS-KENTUCKY4/merlin_170495295_00644ece-a2b4-4898-82a3-7b4056d500f9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/18/us/18VIRUS-KENTUCKY4/merlin_170495295_00644ece-a2b4-4898-82a3-7b4056d500f9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/18/us/18VIRUS-KENTUCKY4/merlin_170495295_00644ece-a2b4-4898-82a3-7b4056d500f9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/18/us/18VIRUS-KENTUCKY4/merlin_170495295_00644ece-a2b4-4898-82a3-7b4056d500f9-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/18/us/18VIRUS-KENTUCKY4/00VIRUS-KENTUCKY5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/18/us/18VIRUS-KENTUCKY4/00VIRUS-KENTUCKY5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/18/us/18VIRUS-KENTUCKY4/00VIRUS-KENTUCKY5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘All Around Us Is Chaos’: Inside a Rural Town Upended by the Virus', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘All Around Us Is Chaos.’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beshear, Andrew G (1977- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kentucky', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cynthiana (Ky)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-17T09:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Rojas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rojas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c84cbd5-7b43-510a-a510-23a8bf974994', 'word_count': 1777, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c84cbd5-7b43-510a-a510-23a8bf974994'}, {'abstract': 'In the time of coronavirus, it’s no longer a rhetorical question.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/17/opinion/coronavirus-trump-biden-sanders.html', 'snippet': 'In the time of coronavirus, it’s no longer a rhetorical question.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bret Stephens: We’re in a new and frightening world, Gail. Every time I get a news alert on my phone, I hear James Earl Jones’s voice in my head, saying, “Mother of God.” And every time I listen to Donald Trump’s voice, I hear Slim Pickens’s voice from “Dr. Strangelove.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/17/opinion/17conversationWeb/17conversationWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 310, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/17/opinion/17conversationWeb/17conversationWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 310}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/17/opinion/17conversationWeb/17conversationWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 529, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/17/opinion/17conversationWeb/17conversationWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1058, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/17/opinion/17conversationWeb/17conversationWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/17/opinion/17conversationWeb/17conversationWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/17/opinion/17conversationWeb/17conversationWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Is There a Wizard Behind the Curtain?', 'kicker': 'The conversation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2020', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 3, '