tname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaufman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/672675c0-3169-5a31-8de3-7de22af90542', 'word_count': 1063, 'uri': 'nyt://article/672675c0-3169-5a31-8de3-7de22af90542'}, {'abstract': 'An excerpt from “Nobody Will Tell You This but Me: A True (as Told to Me) Story,” by Bess Kalb', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/17/books/review/nobody-will-tell-you-this-but-me-a-true-as-told-to-me-story-by-bess-kalb-an-excerpt.html', 'snippet': 'An excerpt from “Nobody Will Tell You This but Me: A True (as Told to Me) Story,” by Bess Kalb', 'lead_paragraph': 'You said your first words to me and you also stood up for the first time when I was there.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Nobody Will Tell You This but Me: A True (as Told to Me) Story,’ by Bess Kalb: An Excerpt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kalb, Bess', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Nobody Will Tell You This But Me: A true (as told to me) story (Book)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-17T09:01:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0eb68dc-d967-5d17-bdb4-5106ffc0f808', 'word_count': 2353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0eb68dc-d967-5d17-bdb4-5106ffc0f808'}, {'abstract': 'An excerpt from “Faster: How a Jewish Driver, an American Heiress, and a Legendary Car Beat Hitler’s Best,” by Neal Bascomb', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/17/books/review/faster-how-a-jewish-driver-an-american-heiress-and-a-legendary-car-beat-hitlers-best-by-neal-bascomb-an-excerpt.html', 'snippet': 'An excerpt from “Faster: How a Jewish Driver, an American Heiress, and a Legendary Car Beat Hitler’s Best,” by Neal Bascomb', 'lead_paragraph': 'The beast, long lurking in plain sight while the Allies stood idle, pounced at last. On May 10, 1940, wave after wave of German bombers, their supercharged engines in high pitch, swept across the dawn sky while armored columns rumbled overland. Into Belgium, Holland, and Luxembourg the Nazis advanced, shattering the morning quiet. Their paratroopers severed communication lines and captured essential bridges. Commandos dropped from glider planes and seized critical fortresses before they could stall any advance. In short order, panzer divisions barreled deep into foreign territory. When French and British forces hurried northeastward to Belgium to stem the attack, they fell straight into the trap of expectations entrenched from the First World War.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Faster: How a Jewish Driver, an American Heiress, and a Legendary Car Beat Hitler’s Best,’ by Neal Bascomb: An Excerpt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "Faster: How a Jewish Driver, an American Heiress, and a Legendary Car Beat Hitler's Best (Book)", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bascomb, Neal', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-17T09:01:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/be836cb7-7ec5-5c8e-ada8-0831a4211d92', 'word_count': 1486, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be836cb7-