', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'French, Erin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Satterfield, Steven', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALASKA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-18T09:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Sifton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sifton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/327d64c7-6349-5a71-9c84-2da628908833', 'word_count': 812, 'uri': 'nyt://article/327d64c7-6349-5a71-9c84-2da628908833'}, {'abstract': 'Anti-vaping groups are stepping into the conversation online — but vapers have already spent years building community there.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/18/magazine/vaping-youtube.html', 'snippet': 'Anti-vaping groups are stepping into the conversation online — but vapers have already spent years building community there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The YouTube video shows two young men sitting in front of a computer screen, enthralled by what they’re watching and pausing, periodically, to marvel at it. They stare as a demonlike character — it resembles something from the costumed metal band Gwar — screams and tries to shred on its guitar. The backdrop behind it shuffles through a series of apocalyptic images: a swirling orange inferno, a black-and-white mushroom cloud, a bunch of explosions. An oil refinery belches smoke as the monster holds a microphone close to his face: “Tons of corrupt filth we keep tossin’,” it belts out, “sending Earth to hell in a pod-shaped coffin.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 