: {'original': 'By Alain de Botton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alain', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'de Botton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/1083d747-450e-52fc-a668-b2444b7b3878', 'word_count': 838, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1083d747-450e-52fc-a668-b2444b7b3878'}, {'abstract': 'The concepts of social distancing and self-quarantine are being interpreted in a variety of ways, not always correctly. Here’s a guide to help you make the right decisions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/19/well/live/coronavirus-quarantine-social-distancing.html', 'snippet': 'The concepts of social distancing and self-quarantine are being interpreted in a variety of ways, not always correctly. Here’s a guide to help you make the right decisions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Dr. Asaf Bitton looked out from his window in Boston recently, he was shocked by the scene. Although schools, offices and businesses already had shut down to slow the spread of coronavirus, the park was packed.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/24/well/well-playground1/merlin_170591526_0f5c5542-5af6-4fe6-8bb6-fdcfdac5de14-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 426, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/24/well/well-playground1/merlin_170591526_0f5c5542-5af6-4fe6-8bb6-fdcfdac5de14-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 426}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/24/well/well-playground1/merlin_170591526_0f5c5542-5af6-4fe6-8bb6-fdcfdac5de14-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 726, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None,