r mobile device:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Do We Vote in a Pandemic?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2020', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-19T09:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/1644d14f-7c31-597b-b079-bb72db2f6b06', 'word_count': 757, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1644d14f-7c31-597b-b079-bb72db2f6b06'}, {'abstract': 'The ableism and ageism being unleashed is its own sort of pestilence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/19/opinion/coronavirus-disabled-health-care.html', 'snippet': 'The ableism and ageism being unleashed is its own sort of pestilence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like many people all over the world, I am not leaving the house now. For me, though, staying home is nothing new. I am in bed as I write this, propped up by my usual heap of cushions, talking to other sick and disabled people all day on my laptop about how the hell we’re going to care for one another in the coming weeks with a gnawing feeling of dread in my belly.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': Non