Epidemics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantines', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-19T09:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elliot Kukla', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elliot', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kukla', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/93065e69-dd6c-57ea-8914-97d79b9ee3d6', 'word_count': 1402, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93065e69-dd6c-57ea-8914-97d79b9ee3d6'}, {'abstract': 'New York’s beloved radio host is part Mister Rogers, part policy wonk. And he’s doing his best to help a city in a pandemic keep its cool.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/19/nyregion/keep-calm-and-listen-to-brian-lehrer.html', 'snippet': 'New York’s beloved radio host is part Mister Rogers, part policy wonk. And he’s doing his best to help a city in a pandemic keep its cool.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brian Lehrer was having difficulty. He was doing his daily radio show from home because of the COVID-19 outbreak. There was a little dead air, and he disconnected a congressman just as he was about to make a point.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/22/nyregion/20lehrer/20lehrer-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/22/nyregion/20lehrer/20lehrer-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/22/nyregion/20lehrer/20lehrer-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/22/nyregion/20lehrer/20lehrer-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/22/nyregion/20lehrer/20lehrer-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/22/nyregion/20lehrer/20lehrer-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/22/nyregion/20lehrer/20lehrer-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Keep Calm and Listen to Brian Lehrer', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Beacon of Calm Helps a City Through the Storms', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radio', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WNYC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lehrer, Brian', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-19T09:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metropolitan', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jazmine Hughes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jazmine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hughes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c29364be-a04d-586f-9baa-142bb91aaf24', 'word_count': 1818, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c29364be-a04d-586f-9baa-142bb91aaf24'}, {'abstract': 'New Yorkers have headed outdoors to the parks to enjoy sunshine and nature — as long as they are 6 feet away from each other.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/19/nyregion/nyc-parks-coronavirus.html', 'snippet': 'New Yorkers have headed outdoors to the parks to enjoy sunshine and nature — as long as they are 6 feet away from each other.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Antsy children, frazzled mothers, seniors strolling on paved paths and young families with newfound free time all shared the familiar green spaces of New York this week as the city shut down around them as a result of the coronavirus spread. Being in a park felt both liberating and subversive, and a public statement of sorts —\xa0one made at least six feet away from stranger and friend alike.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/19/nyregion/19nyvirus-parks4/merlin_170701053_91f8fdfa-601d-4bbc-a945-a8e0a4340e14-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/19/nyregion/19nyvirus-parks4/merlin_170701053_91f8fdfa-601d-4bbc-a945-a8e0a4340e14-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/19/nyregion/19nyvirus-parks4/merlin_170701053_91f8fdfa-601d-4bbc-a945-a8e0a4340e14-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/19/nyregion/19nyvirus-parks4/merlin_170701053_91f8fdfa-601d-4bbc-a945-a8e0a4340e14-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/19/nyregion/19nyvirus-parks4/19nyvirus-parks4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/19/nyregion/19nyvirus-parks4/19nyvirus-parks4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/19/nyregion/19nyvirus-parks4/19nyvirus-parks4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘It Sort of Gives You Hope’: One Place New Yorkers Go to Escape Their Homes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-19T09:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c319b2c8-9ad0-5703-a233-773709c69ff1', 'word_count': 1117, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c319b2c8-9ad0-5703-a233-773709c69ff1'}, {'abstract': 'Let this crisis motivate us to see through the fog of fake individualism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/19/opinion/coronavirus-politics.html', 'snippet': 'Let this crisis motivate us to see through the fog of fake individualism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s a commonplace that emergencies can bring people together. But the imperative issued right now by experts, governments and businesses seems to suggest the very opposite: The sign that you care is that you engage in “social distancing.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/19/opinion/19Mueller/19Mueller-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/19/opinion/19Mueller/19Mueller-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/19/opinion/19Mueller/19Mueller-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/19/opinion/19Mueller/19Mueller-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/19/opinion/19Mueller/19Mueller-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/19/opinion/19Mueller/19Mueller-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/19/opinion/19Mueller/19Mueller-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'We Must Help One Another or Die', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democracy (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Piketty, Thomas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sweden', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-19T09:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jan-Werner Müller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jan-werner', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Müller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/a33029a4-f405-5b2c-995f-aa4b9d9db349', 'word_count': 1064, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a33029a4-f405-5b2c-995f-aa4b9d9db349'}, {'abstract': 'Alarmist is not a word anyone has ever used to describe me before. But this is different.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/19/opinion/coronavirus-doctor-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'Alarmist is not a word anyone has ever used to describe me before. But this is different.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve had hard conversations this week. “Look me in the eye,” I said to my neighbor Karen, who was spiraling to a dark place in her mind. “I make this personal promise to you — I will not let your children die from this disease.” I swallowed back a lump in my throat. Just the image of one of our kids attached to a tube was jarring. Two weeks ago our kids were having a pizza party and watching cartoons together, running back and forth between our apartments. This was before #socialdistancing was trending. Statistically, I still feel good about my promise to Karen because children do not seem to be dying from Covid-19. There are others to whom I cannot make similar promises.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/19/opinion/19Griggs/merlin_170682369_cf8d1e67-f274-4cb7-931e-3f1434985f5f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/19/opinion/19Griggs/merlin_170682369_cf8d1e67-f274-4cb7-931e-3f1434985f5f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/19/opinion/19Griggs/merlin_170682369_cf8d1e67-f274-4cb7-931e-3f1434985f5f-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/19/opinion/19Griggs/merlin_170682369_cf8d1e67-f274-4cb7-931e-3f1434985f5f-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/19/opinion/19Griggs/19Griggs-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/19/opinion/19Griggs/19Griggs-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/19/opinion/19Griggs/19Griggs-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A New York Doctor’s Coronavirus Warning: The Sky Is Falling', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Protective Clothing and Gear', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emergency Medical Treatment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ventilators (Medical)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Medical)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medical Devices', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantines', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-19T09:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cornelia Griggs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cornelia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Griggs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/17ffd3ee-aa8c-53c2-be81-467d889acccb', 'word_count': 1048, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17ffd3ee-aa8c-53c2-be81-467d889acccb'}, {'abstract': 'Only a small minority of people panic under threat, research shows. Far more don’t take the threat seriously enough.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/19/health/coronavirus-panic-anxiety.html', 'snippet': 'Only a small minority of people panic under threat, research shows. Far more don’t take the threat seriously enough.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The sight of empty grocery shelves — widely shared on social media — combined with the dread of an invisible threat seem a perfect recipe for widespread hysteria. But, so far, despite mixed messages from government officials and shortages of tests and hospital capacity, there is little evidence of widespread panic.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/24/science/18SCI-VIRUS-PANIC/merlin_170615766_5ee51e19-3ac9-488f-8e2e-b2c6bf93f43a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/24/science/18SCI-VIRUS-PANIC/merlin_170615766_5ee51e19-3ac9-488f-8e2e-b2c6bf93f43a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/24/science/18SCI-VIRUS-PANIC/merlin_170615766_5ee51e19-3ac9-488f-8e2e-b2c6bf93f43a-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/24/science/18SCI-VIRUS-PANIC/merlin_170615766_5ee51e19-3ac9-488f-8e2e-b2c6bf93f43a-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/24/science/18SCI-VIRUS-PANIC/17VIRUS-PANIC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/24/science/18SCI-VIRUS-PANIC/17VIRUS-PANIC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/24/science/18SCI-VIRUS-PANIC/17VIRUS-PANIC-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Complacency, Not Panic, Is the Real Danger', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Complacency Is a Danger', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shortages', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Erev, Ido', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Anxiety and Stress', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'your-feed-science', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'your-feed-health', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-19T09:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benedict Carey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benedict', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/531391cf-1e8f-58a8-a34c-15c196821a09', 'word_count': 630, 'uri': 'nyt://article/531391cf-1e8f-58a8-a34c-15c196821a09'}, {'abstract': 'Syria became a graveyard, where an aspirational vision of who we are and what we will tolerate now lies. We won’t be immune to the consequences of our failures.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/19/opinion/sunday/syria-war-assad.html', 'snippet': 'Syria became a graveyard, where an aspirational vision of who we are and what we will tolerate now lies. We won’t be immune to the consequences of our failures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When my father died last April in Baltimore, he had finally given up the desire to be buried next to his parents in a cemetery in Damascus, Syria. That he had time to ponder where to be buried was the burden of knowing for several years that he was dying. It was also the luxury, especially for a Syrian, of still having some choice in the matter.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/19/opinion/19Malek1/merlin_169892421_ff46ed9a-1e65-44db-8b88-367a289b347f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/19/opinion/19Malek1/merlin_169892421_ff46ed9a-1e65-44db-8b88-367a289b347f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/19/opinion/19Malek1/merlin_169892421_ff46ed9a-1e65-44db-8b88-367a289b347f-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/19/opinion/19Malek1/merlin_169892421_ff46ed9a-1e65-44db-8b88-367a289b347f-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/19/opinion/19Malek1/19Malek1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/19/opinion/19Malek1/19Malek1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/19/opinion/19Malek1/19Malek1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘He Didn’t Want to Lie in a Grave That Couldn’t Be Visited’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '  Downsizing  Our Dreams for Syria', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Hafez al-', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Damascus (Syria)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-19T09:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alia Malek', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Malek', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/2decad8d-9b7d-57c2-8090-a733ff52d031', 'word_count': 2108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2decad8d-9b7d-57c2-8090-a733ff52d031'}, {'abstract': '“Every time each of us stops, or even just delays, an infection is a small victory.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/19/health/coronavirus-distancing-transmission.html', 'snippet': '“Every time each of us stops, or even just delays, an infection is a small victory.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'After studying infectious diseases, epidemiologists like Helen Jenkins, of Boston University, and Bill Hanage, of Harvard, who are married, typically go one of two ways.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'im