', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jenkins, Helen E', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hanage, William P', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'your-feed-health', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'your-feed-science', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-19T09:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Siobhan Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Siobhan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6626221-08f9-519e-a7a1-4a20490b0ab8', 'word_count': 1491, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6626221-08f9-519e-a7a1-4a20490b0ab8'}, {'abstract': 'Here’s what the federal government must do to help.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/19/opinion/internet-broadband-coronavirus.html', 'snippet': 'Here’s what the federal government must do to help.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One instruction remains consistent and clear during the coronavirus pandemic: Stay home. For many of us, that means taking our daily activities — work, school, medical care and connecting with loved ones — online. But not for everyone. The coming weeks will lay bare the already-cruel reality of the digital divide: tens of millions of Americans cannot access or cannot afford the home broadband connections they need to telework, access medical information and help young people learn when school is closed. When public health requires social distancing and even quarantine, closing the digital divide becomes central to our safety and economic security.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/19/opinion/19Starks/19Starks-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/19/opinion/19Starks/19Starks-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/19/opinion/19Starks/19Starks-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/19/opinion/19Starks/19Starks-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/19/opinion/19Starks/19Starks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/19/opinion/19Starks/19Starks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/19/opinion/19Starks/19Starks-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'To Fight Coronavirus, Millions More Americans Need Internet Access', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rural Areas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stimulus (Economic)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantines', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telemedicine', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Communications Commission', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-19T09:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Geoffrey Starks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Starks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/cba5e1d4-d9af-52de-906f-00f90953f803', 'word_count': 732, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cba5e1d4-d9af-52de-906f-00f90953f803'}, {'abstract': 'The cancellations of the N.C.A.A. tournaments short-circuited the plans of millions to watch basketball this week. The country’s top coaches know where to find good games: digital archives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/19/sports/best-ncaa-tournament-games.html', 'snippet': 'The cancellations of the N.C.A.A. tournaments short-circuited the plans of millions to watch basketball this week. The country’s top coaches know where to find good games: digital archives.', 'lead_paragraph': '“You’re supposed to be watching basketball now,” Muffet McGraw, the women’s basketball coach at Notre Dame, said the other day. “Instead, I’m watching MSNBC and CNN and about to be homebound. That’s not exactly uplifting.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/23/sports/19ncaa-gamestowatch-1/19ncaa-gamestowatch-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name'