w York City and markets tanking, the finance industry is busier than ever — and learning to work from home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Investors, corporations and trading clients are turning to Wall Street amid one of the most tumultuous periods in market history to borrow money, buy or sell assets, and limit losses on existing holdings. But Wall Street itself is grappling with a challenge it had never faced: how to protect employees from a worsening public-health threat while managing clients who need their services around the clock.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/19/business/19wallstreetlife1a/18wallstreetlife1a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/19/business/19wallstreetlife1a/18wallstreetlife1a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/19/business/19wallstreetlife1a/18wallstreetlife1a-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/19/business/19wallstreetlife1a/18wallstreetlife1a-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/19/business/19wallstreetlife1a/18wallstreetlife1a-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/19/business/19wallstreetlife1a/18wallstreetlife1a-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'th