yt://article/2575f8ca-a484-52df-a3e0-59181a03b8d1', 'word_count': 1645, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2575f8ca-a484-52df-a3e0-59181a03b8d1'}, {'abstract': 'Our photographer spent the last two weeks capturing the increasing fragility of New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/19/business/coronavirus-photos-economy.html', 'snippet': 'Our photographer spent the last two weeks capturing the increasing fragility of New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York was still making money a week ago. A few people wearing masks, some closings, but generally business as usual. And then we tumbled down a cliff. By Friday, commuters arriving at Grand Central Terminal paused as they entered the main concourse — stunned by its emptiness, the usual din quieted by stay-at-home orders from companies and the government. For the first time, the vast, star-covered ceiling seemed appropriate.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Witnessing the Birth of the Coronavirus Economy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A City Goes Eerily Quiet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-19T09:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Gilbertson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gilbertson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank'