h', 'byline': {'original': 'By Reed Abelson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Reed', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abelson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86efa88d-7f47-5f23-abf9-bf245e39d970', 'word_count': 1308, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86efa88d-7f47-5f23-abf9-bf245e39d970'}, {'abstract': 'Over 400 years ago, villagers swore to stage the play every decade, as long as God spared them from the plague.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/19/theater/oberammergau-passion-play-coronavirus.html', 'snippet': 'Over 400 years ago, villagers swore to stage the play every decade, as long as God spared them from the plague.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1633, as the plague swept Europe, the villagers of Oberammergau prayed to God. They promised to perform the story of Jesus’s Passion — his life, death and resurrection — every 10 years, as long as God spared them from the horrors of the disease.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/19/arts/19virus-passion-play/19virus-passion-play-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 642, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/19/arts/19virus-passion-play/19virus-passion-play-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 642}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/19/arts/19virus-passion-play/19virus-passion-play-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 958, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/19/arts/19virus-passion-play/19virus-passion-play-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1915, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy':