 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b59f6938-1db1-5512-9517-430f929530cf', 'word_count': 923, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b59f6938-1db1-5512-9517-430f929530cf'}, {'abstract': 'Reinvented menus, lowered prices, fire sales and the good old telephone are enlisted in the fight to survive the coronavirus crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/19/dining/restaurant-delivery-takeout-coronavirus.html', 'snippet': 'Reinvented menus, lowered prices, fire sales and the good old telephone are enlisted in the fight to survive the coronavirus crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like workers in most other fields, restaurant people speak their own language. They talk about covers when they mean customers, sourcing instead of shopping, and cocktail programs, which civilians would just call cocktails. This week, an eerie new term has rippled through the business: contactless delivery.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/19/dining/19virus-takeout06/merlin_170702901_ea9540ec-958e-428b-b1f2-f439fb586368-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/19/dining/19virus-takeout06/merlin_170702901_ea9540ec-958e-428b-b1f2-f439fb586368-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/19/dining/19virus-takeout06/merlin_170702901_ea9540ec-958e-428b-b1f2-f439fb586368-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/19/dining/19virus-takeout06/merlin_170702901_ea9540ec-958e-428b-b1f2-f439fb586368-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/19/dining/19virus-takeout06/00delivery06-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/19/dining/19virus-takeout06/00delivery06-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/19/dining/19virus-takeout06/00delivery06-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'To Stay Afloat, the Restaurant Business Clings to ‘Contactless Delivery’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Contactless Delivery’ Is Just One Innovation Of a Scrambling Sector', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Delivery Services', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bakeries and Baked Products', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Alinea (Chicago, Ill, Restaurant)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bien Cuit (Brooklyn, NY, Bakery)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Huertas (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Seattle (Wash)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-19T16:28:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 's