ction_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shane Goldmacher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldmacher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e54a4cc-6b95-5232-94f7-3c0aacb8ae13', 'word_count': 1603, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e54a4cc-6b95-5232-94f7-3c0aacb8ae13'}, {'abstract': 'Even in war, America has kept up its democratic traditions. We can’t stop now.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/20/opinion/sunday/coronavirus-election-primary-postpone.html', 'snippet': 'Even in war, America has kept up its democratic traditions. We can’t stop now.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Darkness reigned. It was 1864, and the nation was split into two warring camps. Casualties rose steadily — previously unimaginable numbers, ultimately reaching about 750,000 dead — and fighting continued throughout the year. Gen. George McClellan, the Democratic nominee, posed a genuine threat to a second term for Abraham Lincoln. McClellan promised a quick, negotiated end to the war; a Lincoln defeat would have led to a permanently divided nation and the preservation of slavery in the Southern states.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/22/opinion/20Meacham1/merlin_170643612_bc521903-8003-4f2c-b474-6f242139caa1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 408, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/22/opinion/20Meacham1/merlin_170643612_bc521903-8003-4f2c-b474-6f242139caa1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 408}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/22/opinion/20Meacham1/merlin_170643612_bc521903-8003-4f2c-b474-6f242139caa1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 695, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/22/opinion/20Meacham1/merlin_170643612_bc521903-8003-4f2c-b474-6f242139caa1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1391, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/22/opinion/20Meacham1/20Meacham1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/22/opinion/20Meacham1/20Meacham1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/22/opinion/20Meacham1/20Meacham1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'We Can’t Let Coronavirus Postpone Elections', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'We Can’t Let Coronavirus Postpone Elections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2020', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-20T09:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Meacham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Meacham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/a17eb8d7-3ed7-5119-b399-c96c2ac53c89', 'word_count': 1109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a17eb8d7-3ed7-5119-b399-c96c2ac53c89'}, {'abstract': 'From border controls to anti-union efforts, the Trump administration is using the coronavirus to seek policies that the president wanted before the pandemic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/20/us/politics/trump-virus-conservative-policies.html', 'snippet': 'From border controls to anti-union efforts, the Trump administration is using the coronavirus to seek policies that the president wanted before the pandemic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The White House, under the guise of its coronavirus response, is quietly advancing policies that President Trump has long advocated, from tougher border controls to an assault on organized labor to the stonewalling of congressional oversight.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/20/us/politics/20dc-virus-policy-2/20dc-virus-policy-2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/20/us/politics/20dc-virus-policy-2/20dc-virus-policy-2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/20/us/politics/20dc-virus-policy-2/20dc-virus-policy-2-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/20/us/politics/20dc-virus-policy-2/20dc-virus-policy-2-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/20/us/politics/2