': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver-Greenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a551722a-e650-52bf-bd76-6b0f372a3448', 'word_count': 1621, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a551722a-e650-52bf-bd76-6b0f372a3448'}, {'abstract': 'The federal government bungled its response to the coronavirus. But leaders around the country give us reason to hope.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/21/opinion/sunday/coronavirus-governors-cities.html', 'snippet': 'The federal government bungled its response to the coronavirus. But leaders around the country give us reason to hope.', 'lead_paragraph': 'South Korea mobilized health care companies to make coronavirus tests in late January, when the country had only four cases. Soon, 10,000 Koreans a day were being tested, and now new infections are dropping.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Forget the Trump Administration. America Will Save America.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'America, Not Trump,  Will Save America', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Governors (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-21T15:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anne-Marie Slaughter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anne-marie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Slaughter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad0f9af9-c265-5085-b70f-4329be8f98d2', 'word_count': 1975, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad0f9af9-c265-5085-b70f-4329be8f98d2'}, {'abstract': 'If one of the most powerful tech companies can’t call out the president’s dishonesty, who can?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/21/opinion/google-covid-trump.html', 'snippet': 'If one of the most powerful tech companies can’t call out the president’s dishonesty, who can?', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Trump’s handling of the coronavirus pandemic has been a case study in a management style marked by falsehoods and intimidation. Rather than risk inviting his ire, subordinates and fellow Republicans covered for him as he delayed a coordinated response to the coronavirus and it felled nearly 200 Americans.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/20/opinion/20googleWeb/merlin_170478432_94b6f3ad-349c-4e7f-8235-d8062cb63931-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/20/opinion/20googleWeb/merlin_170478432_94b6f3ad-349c-4e7f-8235-d8062cb63931-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 392}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/20/opinion/20googleWeb/merlin_170478432_94b6f3ad-349c-4e7f-8235-d8062cb63931-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/20/opinion/20googleWeb/merlin_170478432_94b6f3ad-349c-4e7f-8235-d8062cb63931-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1337, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/20/opinion/20googleWeb/20googleWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/20/opinion/20googleWeb/20googleWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/20/opinion/20googleWeb/20googleWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Google Gives Cover to Trump’s Lies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rumors and Misinformation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Verily Life Sciences LLC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests (Medical)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Alphabet Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-21T15:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Greg Bensinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Greg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bensinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/221726b5-1270-5a5b-96a2-1dc4f5b11981', 'word_count': 702, 'uri': 'nyt://article/221726b5-1270-5a5b-96a2-1dc4f5b11981'}, {'abstract': 'Congress has all the firepower it needs. It just needs to send spending instructions to the Federal Reserve, as it always does.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/21/opinion/-coronavirus-stimulus-trillion.html', 'snippet': 'Congress has all the firepower it needs. It just needs to send spending instructions to the Federal Reserve, as it always does.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To stem the tide of coronavirus transmission — or “flatten the curve” — Americans have been encouraged to “socially distance” or shelter in place. As a result, our service-based economy, which relies on consumer spending, has seen demand dwindle and commerce grind to a halt.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/21/opinion/21Kelton/merlin_156994575_a8cc5912-fdf1-4f1e-b3f4-4fe9ea2b8c27-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/21/opinion/21Kelton/merlin_156994575_a8cc5912-fdf1-4f1e-b3f4-4fe9ea2b8c27-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/21/opinion/21Kelton/merlin_156994575_a8cc5912-fdf1-4f1e-b3f4-4fe9ea2b8c27-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/21/opinion/21Kelton/merlin_156994575_a8cc5912-fdf1-4f1e-b3f4-4fe9ea2b8c27-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/21/opinion/21Kelton/21Kelton-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/21/opinion/21Kelton/21Kelton-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/21/opinion/21Kelton/21Kelton-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Just Use ‘the Computer’ at the Fed to Give People More Money', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-21T15:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Kelton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kelton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/33ab88ff-6ffe-5b61-9c0f-420b9047ae0a', 'word_count': 1322, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33ab88ff-6ffe-5b61-9c0f-420b9047ae0a'}, {'abstract': 'Voting by mail is key to ensuring the integrity and accessibility of November’s vote.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/21/opinion/sunday/coronavirus-vote-mail.html', 'snippet': 'Voting by mail is key to ensuring the integrity and accessibility of November’s vote.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is no good time for a pandemic to hit. Still, it’s hard to imagine a more vulnerable moment than the one we find ourselves in, only months before some 130 million Americans expected to head to the polls to vote for the next president and thousands of other officeholders. The outcome of the November election could shape the contours of American politics and government for decades.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/22/opinion/22elections_illustration_print_sub/22elections_illustration_print_sub-articleLarge-v5.jpg', 'height': 700, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/22/opinion/22elections_illustration_print_sub/22elections_illustration_print_sub-articleLarge-v5.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 700}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/22/opinion/22elections_illustration_print_sub/22elections_illustration_print_sub-jumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 878, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/22/opinion/22elections_illustration_print_sub/22elections_illustration_print_sub-superJumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1756, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/22/opinion/22elections_illustration_print_sub/22elections_illustration_print_sub-thumbStandard-v6.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/22/opinion/22elections_illustration_print_sub/22elections_illustration_print_sub-thumbStandard-v6.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0,