28:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas L. Friedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Friedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/69ff6c76-e28e-57da-b72f-00f7fdba6419', 'word_count': 2186, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69ff6c76-e28e-57da-b72f-00f7fdba6419'}, {'abstract': 'In a state that until recently had seen more deaths from the coronavirus than any other, the stress has started to multiply. Jobs lost. Kids underfoot. Parents at risk. “It’s exhausting,” one woman said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/22/us/coronavirus-seattle-anxiety-mental-health-stress.html', 'snippet': 'In a state that until recently had seen more deaths from the coronavirus than any other, the stress has started to multiply. Jobs lost. Kids underfoot. Parents at risk. “It’s exhausting,” one woman said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEATTLE — Shannon Koyano is a 39-year-old single mother living, nervously, in the place where the coronavirus got its first deadly foothold in America.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/22/us/22VIRUS-ANXIETY1/22VIRUS-ANXIETY1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/22/us/22VIRUS-ANXIETY1/22VIRUS-ANXIETY1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/22/us/22VIRUS-ANXIETY1/22VIRUS-ANXIETY1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/22/us/22VIRUS-ANXIETY1/22VIRUS-ANXIETY1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/22/us/22VIRUS-ANXIETY1/22VIRUS-ANXIETY1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/22/us/22VIRUS-ANXIETY1/22VIRUS-ANXIETY1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/22/us/22VIRUS-ANXIETY1/22VIRUS-ANXIETY1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Seattle, It Started With Panic. Then the Deeper Anxiety Set In.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Initial Panic Gives Way To Permeating Anxiety In Origin of Outbreak', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Anxiety and Stress', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Seattle (Wash)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (State)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-22T17:36:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Rosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/545ffadd-533b-532e-b3fa-858cf1d92f57', 'word_count': 1754, 'uri': 'nyt://article/545ffadd-533b-532e-b3fa-858cf1d92f57'}, {'abstract': 'The coronavirus outbreak has magnified all kinds of fears. Try living in the moment. Take stock of what’s working. Turn off the television.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/22/us/coronavirus-mental-health-anxiety-tips.html', 'snippet': 'The coronavirus outbreak has magnified all kinds of fears. Try living in the moment. Take stock of what’s working. Turn off the television.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Erasing anxiety from daily life isn’t an option for most people today. But therapists, clergy and meditation specialists say there are simple and accessible ways to overcome debilitating panic.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/20/us/00ANXIETY-TIPS/merlin_170785179_086a836b-32a1-4a62-8bfc-dfafef0f1e17-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/20/us/00ANXIETY-TIPS/merlin_170785179_086a836b-32a1-4a62-8bfc-dfafef0f1e17-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/20/us/00ANXIETY-TIPS/merlin_170785179_086a836b-32a1-4a62-8bfc-dfafef0f1e17-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/20/us/00ANXIETY-TIPS/merlin_170785179_086a836b-32a1-4a62-8bfc-dfafef0f1e17-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/20/us/00ANXIETY-TIPS/00ANXIETY-TIPS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_