', 'rank': 19, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shortages', 'rank': 20, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Contracts and Procurement', 'rank': 21, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-22T23:59:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By David E. Sanger, Ana Swanson and Maggie Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Sanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Swanson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Maggie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/007696e6-664f-5a10-897c-3dbf83c25de1', 'word_count': 1685, 'uri': 'nyt://article/007696e6-664f-5a10-897c-3dbf83c25de1'}, {'abstract': 'Medical shortages are his responsibility.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/22/opinion/trump-coronavirus.html', 'snippet': 'Medical shortages are his responsibility.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At a private New York meeting in October of 1940, William Knudsen made a desperate plea to the automobile industry’s top executives. Knudsen himself had been the president of General Motors until a few months earlier. But he had stepped down to help oversee military production at President Franklin Roosevelt’s request. The position paid $1 a year.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/22/opinion/22Leonhardt/merlin_170849976_15e30554-e5cb-4b4d-a7c0-701c306d6bfe-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_nam