jor': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Planned Parenthood Federation of America', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-23T23:02:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sabrina Tavernise', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sabrina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tavernise', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/959565b8-d22a-551a-bc68-620982c9c2ce', 'word_count': 818, 'uri': 'nyt://article/959565b8-d22a-551a-bc68-620982c9c2ce'}, {'abstract': '“How we spend our days is how we spend our lives.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/23/smarter-living/why-mundane-moments-matter.html', 'snippet': '“How we spend our days is how we spend our lives.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'My mother and I have sipped tea with maharanis, swapped stories with Burmese nuns and bumped through the streets of Bangkok on midnight tuk tuks — but the delight we return to, again and again, is the moon. “Go outside and take a look,” she’ll command over text, and I’ll stumble out the door to glimpse at a crescent sliver. We swap cellphone photos of fuzzy white discs that are indistinguishable from the ones that preceded them but offer what feels like newfound delight. Our shared moon: a simple joy that binds us together across years and over continents.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/20/smarter-living/00sl-mundan-2/00sl-mundan-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 418, 'width': 600, 'subT