}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fauci, Anthony S', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pence, Mike', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'White House Building (Washington, DC)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-23T23:19:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Karni', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Karni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d12f1f41-72f0-506c-8d36-913a766f055d', 'word_count': 1346, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d12f1f41-72f0-506c-8d36-913a766f055d'}, {'abstract': 'These shot glasses let you mete out precious liquors, and come in handy for baking projects.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/23/dining/williams-sonoma-shot-glass-measuring-cup.html', 'snippet': 'These shot glasses let you mete out precious liquors, and come in handy for baking projects.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You need a drink, but you — not some mixologist — are in charge. Though professionals prefer little metal measuring containers, this set of one-and-a-half ounce glass ones, with markings for a half-ounce and an ounce, is very easy to use. And having several means that you can combine multiple spirits without rinsing in between. They’re also superb for pouring measured drams of precious Pappy Van Winkle. Use them for baking and cooking, keeping in mind that one-half ounce is a tablespoon.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/25/dining/23burner-shot/23burner-shot-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 355, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/25/dining/23burner-shot/23burner-shot-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 355}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/25/dining/23burner-shot/23burner-shot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 606, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/25/dining/23burner-shot/23burner-shot-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1212, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/25/dining/23burner-shot/23burner-shot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/25/dining/23burner-shot/23burner-shot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/25/dining/23burner-shot/23burner-shot-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Handy Measure', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Make a Cocktail,  Or Perhaps a Cake', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Williams-Sonoma Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weights and Measures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-23T23:23:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2fedf2f0-c1f8-526c-ae5c-10e3bfa7325d', 'word_count': 126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2fedf2f0-c1f8-526c-ae5c-10e3bfa7325d'}, {'abstract': 'The meals, which serve two to four, are available at Blue Hill at Stone Barns.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/23/dining/dan-barber-blue-hill-meal-kits.html', 'snippet': 'The meals, which serve two to four, are available at Blue Hill at Stone Barns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like a number of other chefs and restaurants, Dan Barber, the chef and an owner of Blue Hill in Manhattan, and Blue Hill at Stone Barns in Westchester County, is assembling market boxes for pickup. Each will contain ingredients and cooking instructions for a dish that will serve two to four people. Though the ingredients will vary daily, you can count on a rich broth as one of the components, along with fresh and fermented vegetables, meats, eggs and a flatbread made with freshly milled flour. They are meant to keep the restaurant staff and local farmers employed. The ingredients and recipe will change weekly.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/25/dining/25Burner-Box-B/merlin_170772906_18017288-11e6-46ac-92a9-760d402019fc-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/25/dining/25Burner-Box-B/merlin_170772906_18017288-11e6-46ac-92a9-760d402019fc-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/25/dining/25Burner-Box-B/merlin_170772906_18017288-11e6-46ac-92a9-760d402019fc-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/25/dining/25Burner-Box-B/merlin_170772906_18017288-11e6-46ac-92a9-760d402019fc-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/25/dining/25Burner-Box-B/merlin_170772906_18017288-11e6-46ac-92a9-760d402019fc-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/25/dining/25Burner-Box-B/merlin_170772906_18017288-11e6-46ac-92a9-760d402019fc-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/25/dining/25Burner-Box-B/merlin_170772906_18017288-11e6-46ac-92a9-760d402019fc-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Meal Kits From the Chef Dan Barber', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Supply: Meal Kits From the Chef Dan Barber', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Blue Hill (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Blue Hill at Stone Barns (Pocantico Hills, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barber, Dan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-23T23:26:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06fe79c4-bfc9-5e13-a9ec-455d97819a50', 'word_count': 150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06fe79c4-bfc9-5e13-a9ec-455d97819a50'}, {'abstract': 'Lil Bucks, a sprouted buckwheat snack, adds a touch of flavor to granola, yogurt or salads.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/23/dining/lil-bucks-sprouted-buckwheat.html', 'snippet': 'Lil Bucks, a sprouted buckwheat snack, adds a touch of flavor to granola, yogurt or salads.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s nothing new about buckwheat, a seed (not really a grain) that’s most comfortable growing in cooler and high-altitude climates worldwide. But the form in which Emily Griffith is selling them is innovative. While living in Australia, she discovered sprouted buckwheat and created Lil Bucks, a company to make and sell the crunchy, earthy-tasting seeds. You can add them to granola, sprinkle them on salad, dust them over yogurt and so forth. Like so much these days, they’re billed as a “superfood,” but the real benefit is their fiber (5 grams in a quarter-cup), protein (6 grams in a quarter-cup), their nice texture and alluring flavor. In addition to plain, they also come flavored with matcha or cacao, neither of which add much in my view. Chunky clusters with other seeds and seasoned with chocolate or turmeric-lemon myrtle are for snacking.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/25/dining/23burner-buck/23burner-buck-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 329, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/25/dining/23burner-buck/23burner-buck-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 329}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/25/dining/23burner-buck/23burner-buck-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 562, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/25/dining/23burner-buck/23burner-buck-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1124, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/25/dining/23burner-buck/23burner-buck-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/25/dining/23burner-buck/23burner-buck-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/25/dining/23burner-buck/23burner-buck-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Add a Sprinkle to Breakfast', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Fortify: Buckwheat That Works As a Snack or a Sprinkle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snack Foods', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lil Bucks LLC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-23T23:27:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf9316cf-df25-5632-8378-a484ec48027b', 'word_count': 185, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf9316cf-df25-5632-8378-a484ec48027b'}, {'abstract': '“The Japanese Table,” a new book by a Swedish cook smitten with Japan, offers nourishing, small-scale ideas for dinner.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/23/dining/japanese-table-book-sofia-hellsten.html', 'snippet': '“The Japanese Table,” a new book by a Swedish cook smitten with Japan, offers nourishing, small-scale ideas for dinner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sofia Hellsten is Swedish, but, having lived in Japan, she’s devoted to Japanese food and dining. Her new book explores the simple everyday meals she craves, especially when not in Japan. They’re the sort of nourishing, comforting plates that are easily made and frequently feature vegetables. They’re also enjoyable to serve one or two but no more than four: perfect for troubled times in sequestered households. It’s hard to resist rice, egg and scallions in a soft, single-serving porridge; tamago omelet as egg salad in a sandwich, with miso mayonnaise; silky eggplant with miso; cod with sweet miso that might have been the ur-black cod recipe made famous by Nobu; and somen noodles in a well-seasoned dashi broth. The book does a fine job of explaining Japanese green teas, and there’s a pantry list of staples, most of which are sold online.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/25/dining/23burner/merlin_170747742_94ea90d3-07e1-4acd-a1f2-df6c106849a6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 814, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/25/dining/23burner/merlin_170747742_94ea90d3-07e1-4acd-a1f2-df6c106849a6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 814}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 