alue': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-24T05:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sara Aridi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Aridi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a11a7af-6ce7-52a0-9773-0cfbc2198798', 'word_count': 482, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a11a7af-6ce7-52a0-9773-0cfbc2198798'}, {'abstract': 'Tehran doesn’t have the resources to enforce quarantines and take other measures to contain the outbreak.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/24/opinion/iran-sanctions-coronavirus.html', 'snippet': 'Tehran doesn’t have the resources to enforce quarantines and take other measures to contain the outbreak.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The toll of the eight-year war between Iran and Iraq, which killed as many as one million people in the 1980s, is feared to pale in comparison to that of the coronavirus epidemic: Iranian researchers have estimated that the outbreak, which has already killed more than 1,500 people in the country, will peak around late May and could result in 3.5 million deaths.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/24/opinion/24bajoghlirouhi/merlin_170854482_f7fbcbb2-52f8-404b-9539-685cee4323e4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/24/opinion/24bajoghlirouhi/merlin_170854482_f7fbcbb2-52f8-404b-9539-685cee4323e4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/24/opinion/24bajoghlirouhi/merlin_170854482_f7fbcbb2-52f8-404b-9539-685cee43