 doesn’t have to be a mystery or a battle of wills.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Having a child who won’t nap is frustrating during the best of times. But being locked in a house with a grumpy, screaming toddler during a lockdown or social distancing is torture. Scientists tell us that naps improve children’s moods, help them learn better and even reduce their risk of injury.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Your Kids Refuse to Nap? There’s Hope', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Here to Help; What to Do When a Child Refuses to Nap', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sleep', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Youth', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Day Care Centers', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (Pre-School)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-24T16:26:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Parenting', 'section_name': 'Parenting', 'byline': {'original': 'By Craig Canapari, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Craig', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Canapari', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bb937e2-e9a4-583b-93bc-95027e7c2d42', 'word_count': 1269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bb937e2-e9a4-583b-93bc-95027e7c2d42'}, {'abstract': 'With ridership and revenues plummeting, New York’s transportation system needs an urgent infusion of federal money.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/24/opinion/mta-new-york-transit.html', 'snippet': 'With ridership and revenues plummeting, New York’s transportation system needs an urgent infusion of federal money.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While the country responds to the Covid-19 pandemic, mass-transit employees continue to show up day after day to ensure that emergency medical workers and other critical personnel can do their jobs for the people of New York. That’s why it’s so disheartening to watch as some in Washington use mass-transit funding as political currency.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/24/opinion/24foyeWeb/merlin_170882184_14f2ad0d-72ea-478e-a0c2-92f34546b85f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/24/opinion/24foyeWeb/merlin_170882184_14f2ad0d-72ea-478e-a0c2-92f34546b85f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/24/opinion/24foyeWeb/merlin_170882184_14f2ad0d-72ea-478e-a0c2-92f34546b85f-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/24/opinion/24foyeWeb/merlin_170882184_14f2ad0d-72ea-478e-a0c2-92f34546b85f-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/24/opinion/24foyeWeb/24foyeWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/24/opinion/24foyeWeb/24foyeWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'th