w', 'section_name': 'Briefing', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melina Delkic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Delkic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'briefing', '_id': 'nyt://article/56bd27a1-d518-577f-8af2-53d8d70ed4d2', 'word_count': 1503, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56bd27a1-d518-577f-8af2-53d8d70ed4d2'}, {'abstract': 'Modern Love in miniature, featuring reader-submitted stories of no more than 100 words.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/24/style/tiny-modern-love-stories-coronavirus-in-his-bed.html', 'snippet': 'Modern Love in miniature, featuring reader-submitted stories of no more than 100 words.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If a pandemic cancels the remainder of your spring semester, and your recent ex decides to suspend the rules of your breakup in case “the apocalypse” keeps you apart forever, and you find yourself lying once again in his bed, your faces flushed, the afternoon humming by outside, take your time with leaving. The future will charge onward, but for now you can allow the memory of other lazy days you spent in this bed to envelop you entirely. You would like to believe this feeling transcends whatever comes next. For an hour or two, it does. — Lily Goldberg', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/04/fashion/04TINYLOVE-ILLO1/04TINYLOVE-ILLO1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/04/04/fashion/04TINYLOVE-ILLO1/04TINYLOVE-ILLO1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/04/fashion/04TINYLOVE-ILLO1/04TINYLOVE-ILLO1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/04/fashion/04TINYLOVE-ILLO1/04TINYLOVE-ILLO1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/04/fashion/04TINYLOVE-ILLO1/04TINYLOVE-ILLO1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/04/04/fashion/04TINYLOVE-ILLO1/04TINYLOVE-ILLO1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/04/fashion/04TINYLOVE-ILLO1/04TINYLOVE-ILLO1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tiny Love Stories: ‘You Find Yourself Lying Once Again in His Bed’', 'kicker': 'Modern Love', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Love (Emotion)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Modern Love (Times Column)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Relationships', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Text Messaging', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Retirement Communities and Assisted Living', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-24T19:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24a3b771-3d41-5389-bf77-278b0b127620', 'word_count': 478, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24a3b771-3d41-5389-bf77-278b0b127620'}, {'abstract': 'The coronavirus will ravage the country’s already devastated health system.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/24/opinion/venezuela-coronavirus.html', 'snippet': 'The coronavirus will ravage the country’s already devastated health system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ÁVILA, Spain — In this small city about an hour northwest of Madrid, the streets are deserted, the emergency rooms are on the brink of collapse, and anxiety and fear are everywhere. It all feels very familiar.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/24/opinion/24Cantor/merlin_170885829_bf779697-14ca-44ec-87b2-8d9d37ea358e-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/24/opinion/24Cantor/merlin_170885829_bf779697-14ca-44ec-87b2-8d9d37ea358e-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/24/opinion/24Cantor/merlin_170885829_bf779697-14ca-44ec-87b2-8d9d37ea358e-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/24/opinion/24Cantor/merlin_170885829_bf779697-14ca-44ec-87b2-8d9d37ea358e-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/24/opinion/24Cantor/24Cantor-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/24/opinion/24Cantor/24Cantor-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/24/opinion/24Cantor/24Cantor-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Whenever I Throw Away a Mask, I Think of Venezuela and I Freak Out', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Health Organization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venezuela', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-24T19:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Astrid Cantor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Astrid', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cantor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/319255b7-ddc4-50a5-8346-69006a87623d', 'word_count': 1018, 'uri': 'nyt://article/319255b7-ddc4-50a5-8346-69006a87623d'}, {'abstract': 'Be kind. Don’t let the weight of your grief and anger fall on our shoulders.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/24/opinion/grocery-store-covid.html', 'snippet': 'Be kind. Don’t let the weight of your grief and anger fall on our shoulders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CLEVELAND — For the last two years, I have worked two jobs: one full-time position in food service at a grocery store, and one part-time as a receptionist at a hair salon. I took five days off in October to get married, and I haven’t had a vacation longer than that since 2017. I’ve worked every major holiday since then, too.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'typ