lly be worse. Imagine if, next week, we find that coronavirus infection has spread so far through major supply lines as to sicken large numbers of the workers who deliver goods and also begins to threaten their recipients. Or imagine what the economy would look like if broadband internet service were to go down for significant parts of the population.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/25/opinion/25Wu/merlin_170617449_6c16b502-7f5c-4ed6-a846-e3ad725f5a78-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/25/opinion/25Wu/merlin_170617449_6c16b502-7f5c-4ed6-a846-e3ad725f5a78-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/25/opinion/25Wu/merlin_170617449_6c16b502-7f5c-4ed6-a846-e3ad725f5a78-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/25/opinion/25Wu/merlin_170617449_6c16b502-7f5c-4ed6-a846-e3ad725f5a78-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/25/opinion/25Wu/25Wu-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/25/opinion/25Wu/25Wu-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/25/opinion/25Wu/25Wu-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'We Need to Protect the ‘Touchless Economy’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Protect Our  ‘Touchless  Economy’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Delivery Services', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Postal Service and Post Offices', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Supermarkets and Grocery Stores', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-25T09:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Wu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/c340f4d0-b9e0-5b87-8372-69e0445ea213', 'word_count': 855, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c340f4d0-b9e0-5b87-8372-69e0445ea213'}, {'abstract': 'For those used to luxuriating in salons, now waxing, hair dye and facials have come home and online.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/25/style/home-beauty-treatmentsdiy-tutorials-are-what-we-watch-now.html', 'snippet': 'For those used to luxuriating in salons, now waxing, hair dye and facials have come home and online.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the last couple of weeks, some shoppers have been stocking up on more than just soap and pasta. For those who are able and healthy and who look at self-care like home improvement — necessary to maintaining both standards and self-regard — a different type of staple has become essential to get through the socially distanced days ahead.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/26/fashion/25SKIN-ATHOME/25SKIN-ATHOME-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 657, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/26/fashion/25SKIN-ATHOME/25SKIN-ATHOME-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 657}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/26/fashion/25SKIN-ATHOME/25SKIN-ATHOME-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 935, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/26/fashion/25SKIN-ATHOME/25SKIN-ATHOME-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1870, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/26/fashion/25SKIN-ATHOME/25SKIN-ATHOME-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/26/fashion/25SKIN-ATHOME/25SKIN-ATHOME-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/26/fashion/25SKIN-ATHOME/25SKIN-ATHOME-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Salon Comes to Your Home, and to Your iPad', 'kicker': 'Skin Deep', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Salons on Your iPad', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beauty Salons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Face', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hair', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nails (Body Part)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cosmetics and Toiletries', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantines', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-25T09:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Felder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Felder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/695bdcbb-23e2-5c07-9c84-7d2562469a10', 'word_count': 847, 'uri': 'nyt://article/695bdcbb-23e2-5c07-9c84-7d2562469a10'}, {'abstract': 'For too long, mothers have been held responsible for every aspect of their children’s well-being.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/25/opinion/coronavirus-parenting.html', 'snippet': 'For too long, mothers have been held responsible for every aspect of their children’s well-being.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I couldn’t sleep on the night of March 12. New York City public schools were still open, and many of my peers were choosing to pull their children out. I couldn’t decide whether to keep mine in class. My friends in Hong Kong had been home with their kids for months, but the schools never closed in Singapore.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/25/opinion/25Grose2/25Grose2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 809, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/25/opinion/25Grose2/25Grose2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 809}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/25/opinion/25Grose2/25Grose2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 760, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/25/opinion/25Grose2/25Grose2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1520, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/25/opinion/25Grose2/25Grose2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/25/opinion/25Grose2/25Grose2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/25/opinion/25Grose2/25Grose2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Coronavirus Exposes the Great Lie of Modern Motherhood', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-25T09:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jessica Grose', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grose', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/05a0ec45-e583-52c6-8977-ff104975e654', 'word_count': 1120, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05a0ec45-e583-52c6-8977-ff104975e654'}, {'abstract': 'Muscles may “remember” in ways that will allow us to regain fitness once gyms reopen and we start working out again.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/25/well/move/coronavirus-exercise-muscles-fitness.html', 'snippet': 'Muscles may “remember” in ways that will allow us to regain fitness once gyms reopen and we start working out again.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For those of us sheltering at home because of coronavirus and unable to visit the gym or otherwise weight train — which, right now, is most of us — a new study of the inner workings of our muscles should be heartening. It finds that if muscles have been trained in the past, they seem to develop a molecular memory of working out that lingers through a prolonged period of inactivity, and once we start training again, this “muscle memory” could speed the process by which we regain our former muscular strength and size.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/31/well/physed-muscle-photo/physed-muscle-photo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/31/well/physed-muscle-photo/physed-muscle-photo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/31/well/physed-muscle-photo/physed-muscle-photo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/31/well/physed-muscle-photo/physed-muscle-photo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJ