yt://article/afedecda-e1e5-5fd9-9180-043d094ee9fa'}, {'abstract': 'The coronavirus pandemic has inspired us to connect with one another while social distancing, no screens required.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/25/opinion/coronavirus-scream.html', 'snippet': 'The coronavirus pandemic has inspired us to connect with one another while social distancing, no screens required.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few days into social distancing, I learned my daughters’ school would be closed indefinitely. And as the school where I teach had crash-landed into its own eerie spring break, the walls of my house started to close in. My wife and I set up Google Hangout and Google Meet, and weighed the prospects of third-grade virtual reading groups and of all the screen time our daughters might have as we slouched toward our de-limbed lives.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/25/opinion/25Donahue/25Donahue-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/25/opinion/25Donahue/25Donahue-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/25/opinion/25Donahue/25Donahue-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/25/opinion/25Donahue/25Donahue-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/25/opinion/25Donahue/25Donahue-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/25/opinion/25Donahue/25Donahue-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/25/opinion/25Donahue/25Donahue-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'My Coronavirus Routine: A Neighborhood Primal Scream', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emotions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-25T19:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Donahue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Donahue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d934e32-8f24-5fc8-a4cb-62ae0bae2892', 'word_count': 977, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d934e32-8f24-5fc8-a4cb-62ae0bae2892'}, {'abstract': 'I created a cooperative game to encourage people to play together. Covid-19 is making it more relevant than ever.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/25/opinion/pandemic-game-covid.html', 'snippet': 'I created a cooperative game to encourage people to play together. Covid-19 is making it more relevant than ever.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our new reality became very immediate for my wife Donna and me in late February, when she came down with nasty, flulike symptoms and couldn’t get tested for the coronavirus for four long weeks. When she finally did, we were relieved the test came back negative.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York 