}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1611c650-78de-5f27-9a2f-fdbc51186694', 'word_count': 1245, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1611c650-78de-5f27-9a2f-fdbc51186694'}, {'abstract': 'Despite some obvious suspects, scientists say chance may have played a big role in the explosion of cases.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/26/health/coronavirus-nyc-spread.html', 'snippet': 'Despite some obvious suspects, scientists say chance may have played a big role in the explosion of cases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Perhaps it was inevitable that New York City and its suburbs would become an epicenter of the coronavirus epidemic in the United States. The population density, reliance on public transportation and constant influx of tourists — all would seem to make the metropolitan area a target.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/25/science/25VIRUS-NYC1/25VIRUS-NYC1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/25/science/25VIRUS-NYC1/25VIRUS-NYC1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/25/science/25VIRUS-NYC1/25VIRUS-NYC1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/25/science/25VIRUS-NYC1/25VIRUS-NYC1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/25/science/25VIRUS-NYC1/25VIRUS-NYC1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStanda