: 'Estate planning lawyers we talked to this week said they had been getting more calls since the outbreak worsened.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Joel Solomon sold his financial services firm in mid-January, he had been planning to call his estate lawyer to update his will and trusts. But with coronavirus cases spiking, Mr. Solomon and his wife, Nancy, decided to act immediately.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/27/business/26VIRUS-ESTATES-print/26ESTATES-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/27/business/26VIRUS-ESTATES-print/26ESTATES-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/27/business/26VIRUS-ESTATES-print/26ESTATES-01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/27/business/26VIRUS-ESTATES-print/26ESTATES-01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/27/business/26VIRUS-ESTATES-print/26ESTATES-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/27/business/26VIRUS-ESTATES-print/26ESTATES-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/27/business/26VIRUS-ESTATES-print/26ESTATES-01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What to Know About Making a Will in the Age of Coronavirus', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Making a Will (or Updating One) Just Became More Complex', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Living Wills and Health Care Proxies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wills and Estates', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantines', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Retirement', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-26T16:53:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan B. Garland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a6aa06b-3c35-597a-90af-c8a1dd3aa116', 'word_count': 1793, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a6aa06b-3c35-597a-90af-c8a1dd3aa116'}, {'abstract': 'Disruptions in routines and the need for hands-on care are among the special challenges for dementia patients and their caregivers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/26/well/family/coronavirus-dementia-patients-caregivers.html', 'snippet': 'Disruptions in routines and the need for hands-on care are among the special challenges for dementia patients and their caregivers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the coronavirus advances, it is taking a particularly harsh toll on the many who are caring for a loved one with dementia or Alzheimer’s, the most common form of dementia. According to a report by the Alzheimer’s Association, more than 16 million Americans are providing unpaid care for those with Alzheimer’s or other types of dementia. For them the virus is “really a double whammy,” said Lynn Friss Feinberg, a senior strategic policy adviser at AARP’s Public Policy Institute. “You’re worrying about your own health and that of your family member.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/26/well/26well-dementia2/26well-dementia2-articleLarge.png', 'height': 376, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/26/well/26well-dementia2/26well-dementia2-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 376}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/26/well/26well-dementia2/26well-dementia2-jumbo.png', 'height': 604, 'width': 964, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/26/well/26well-dementia2/26well-dementia2-superJumbo.png', 'height': 604, 'width': 964, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/26/well/26well-dementia2/26well-dementia2-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/26/well/26well-dementia2/26well-dementia2-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/26/well/26well-dementia2/26well-dementia2-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Dementia Meets the Coronavirus Crisis', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Alzheimer's Disease", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dementia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Home Health Care', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-26T16:57:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Well', 'section_name': 'Well', 'subsection_name': 'Family', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Halpert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Halpert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/daf7f64b-fe90-5601-a1c0-497ce9892ef0', 'word_count': 1242, 'uri': 'nyt://article/daf7f64b-fe90-5601-a1c0-497ce9892ef0'}, {'abstract': 'When theaters closed by the pandemic stream their shuttered plays online, watching sharpens the longing for the real thing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/26/theater/streaming-theater.html', 'snippet': 'When theaters closed by the pandemic stream their shuttered plays online, watching sharpens the longing for the real thing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I wanted to climb right through the screen into a seat a few rows from the stage.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/27/arts/25SIBLINGS-STREAM-1/merlin_170934651_534d8bf2-9574-4e57-a099-25716e7d7f91-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/27/arts/25SIBLINGS-STREAM-1/merlin_170934651_534d8bf2-9574-4e57-a099-25716e7d7f91-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xl