n treating anxiety, offered simple and soothing advice that has come to influence much of our approach to panic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/26/books/hope-help-for-your-nerves-claire-weekes-virus.html', 'snippet': 'Claire Weekes, a pioneer in treating anxiety, offered simple and soothing advice that has come to influence much of our approach to panic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I felt the rumblings of a panic attack just now, while I was typing. It starts with a burning sensation in my temples. My chest tightens up a little, suddenly corseted, and my vision tunnels like one of those old Western photos in which everyone is grim-faced. That is merely the prequel.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/04/books/26NERVES/26NERVES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/04/04/books/26NERVES/26NERVES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/04/books/26NERVES/26NERVES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/04/books/26NERVES/26NERVES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/04/books/26NERVES/26NERVES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/04/04/books/26NERVES/26NERVES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/04/books/26NERVES/26NERVES-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Desperately Seeking Hope and Help for Your Nerves? Try Reading ‘Hope and Help for Your Nerves’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Calm Your Disquiet By Embracing It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Anxiety and Stress', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Hope and Help for Your Nerves (Book)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weekes, Claire (1903-90)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-26T17:53:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hillary Kelly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hillary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kelly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68764502-a4cd-52bd-87db-32748b010ebc', 'word_count': 1270, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68764502-a4cd-52bd-87db-32748b010ebc'}, {'abstract': 'Tarsila do Amaral’s drawings are among dozens of landscapes of Brazil you can view from home. Ditto with Guanyu Xu’s photo installations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/26/arts/design/new-york-art-galleries.html', 'snippet': 'Tarsila do Amaral’s drawings are among dozens of landscapes of Brazil you can view from home. Ditto with Guanyu Xu’s photo installations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lecturing in Buenos Aires two years ago, the novelist J.M. Coetzee — born in South Africa, now a citizen of Australia, and teaching regularly in Argentina — argued that the southern hemisphere has a big problem: Its artists and writers can only win global attention by pleasing “the cultural gatekeepers of the metropoles of the north,” who “decide which stories by the south about itself will be accepted.” It’s exactly these contesting gazes on the spaces of the south, by colonizers and colonized, that animate a rich exhibition staged by the Brazilian gallery Mendes Wood DM at its New York outpost.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/27/arts/26galleries-landscape1/merlin_170793975_3fbcc981-f28d-49d5-906d-e816a6e605dc-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 606, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/27/arts/26galleries-landscape1/merlin_170793975_3fbcc981-f28d-49d5-906d-e816a6e605dc-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 606}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/27/arts/26galleries-landscape1/merlin_170793975_3fbcc981-f28d-49d5-906d-e816a6e605dc-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1015, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/27/arts/26galleries-landscape1/merlin_170793975_3fbcc981-f28d-49d5-906d-e816a6e605dc-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2029, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/27/arts/26galleries-landscape1/merlin_170793975_3fbcc981-f28d-49d5-906d-e816a6e605dc-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/27/arts/26galleries-landscape1/merlin_170793975_3fbcc981-f28d-49d5-906d-e816a6e605dc-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth