etter to see this great flutter of planes, volumes and edges in person. But an online visit is the next best thing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Donald Judd’s large, untitled installation piece in unfinished plywood at Gagosian Gallery is a plain-spoken giant that, surprisingly, has quite a bit to say. In its complexity and openness, it seems like almost nothing else Judd (1928-1994) ever made, and it hasn’t been seen in New York since 1981, when it debuted at the Castelli Gallery in SoHo a year after its completion.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/27/arts/26galleries-judd/26galleries-judd-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 454, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/27/arts/26galleries-judd/26galleries-judd-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 454}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/27/arts/26galleries-judd/26galleries-judd-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 774, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/27/arts/26galleries-judd/26galleries-judd-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1480, 'width': 1957, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/27/arts/26galleries-judd/26galleries-judd-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/27/arts/26galleries-judd/26galleries-judd-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/27/arts/26galleries-judd/26galleries-judd-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Donald Judd’s Plain-Spoken Masterpiece', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Plain-Spoken Masterpiece', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Judd, Donald', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gagosian Gallery', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-26T18:22:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8e2e0aa-13ca-5d47-90d2-8c5ac0f345cf', 'word_count': 548, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8e2e0aa-13ca-5d47-90d2-8c5ac0f345cf'}, {'abstract': 'For the third time in five years, abnormally warm water has caused a “mass bleaching” of coral, and some of it will not survive. Scientists say global warming is killing reefs worldwide.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/26/world/australia/bleaching-great-barrier-reef.html', 'snippet': 'For the third time in five years, abnormally warm water has caused a “mass bleaching” of coral, and some of it will not survive. Scientists say global warming is killing reefs worldwide.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Record-breaking warm waters have bleached large parts of Australia’s Great Barrier Reef this year, as they did in 2016 and 2017, scientists reported on Thursday — the latest sign that global warming threatens the health of one of the world’s most important marine ecosystems.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/26/world/26reef/merlin_165467121_5eaa5f74-8e8e-4a64-b630-434fd8e8ed8c-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/26/world/26reef/merlin_165467121_5eaa5f74-8e8e-4a64-b630-434fd8e8ed8c-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/26/world/26reef/merlin_165467121_5eaa5f74-8e8e-4a64-b630-434fd8e8ed8c-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/26/world/26reef/merlin_165467121_5eaa5f74-8e8e-4a64-b630-434fd8e8ed8c-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/26/world/26reef/26reef-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/26/world/26reef/26reef-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/26/world/26reef/26reef-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Australia’s Record Heat Means Another Blow to Great Barrier Reef', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Climate Crisis Ravages Great Barrier Reef With 3rd Mass Bleaching Event in 5 Years', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Barrier Reef (Australia)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reefs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coral', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Indigenous Australians', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-26T18:24:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Australia', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Pérez-Peña', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pérez-Peña', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe3b9898-4fe8-584b-9231-692c6117265e', 'word_count': 599, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe3b9898-4fe8-584b-9231-692c6117265e'}, {'abstract': 'As the pandemic sequesters millions at home, an emerging category of intimate news programs offers a comforting voice.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/26/arts/daily-podcasts-coronavirus.html', 'snippet': 'As the pandemic sequesters millions at home, an emerging category of intimate news programs offers a comforting voice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When it’s time to get to work, after a morning teleconference and a cup (or two) of coffee, Cardiff Garcia combs his hair, heads into the closet of his Upper West Side apartment and hangs a blanket over his head. Waiting for his FaceTime call is Stacey Vanek Smith, who answers from a makeshift fort — her own blanket, stretched over two side chairs — that she rebuilds each day in her Brooklyn living room.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': N