 {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tokyo (Japan)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-27T15:39:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38b3ec3f-8cdc-5e41-8628-496f3e7db9a7', 'word_count': 1007, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38b3ec3f-8cdc-5e41-8628-496f3e7db9a7'}, {'abstract': 'Helped by a raft of strong women, the heroine of Kate Messner’s “Chirp” reclaims the parts of her childhood she’s not ready to leave behind.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/27/books/review/chirp-kate-messner.html', 'snippet': 'Helped by a raft of strong women, the heroine of Kate Messner’s “Chirp” reclaims the parts of her childhood she’s not ready to leave behind.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Kate Messner’s resonant, necessary CHIRP (Bloomsbury, 227 pp., $16.99; ages 8 to 12), 12-year-old Mia is on the mend — from a broken arm, after a fall from the balance beam, and more slowly, from the psychic scars left by a predatory coach.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/29/books/review/29-BKS-TUCKER_KIDS/29-BKS-TUCKER_KIDS-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 755, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/29/books/review/29-BKS-TUCKER_KIDS/29-BKS-TUCKER_KIDS-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 755, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/29/books/review/29-BKS-TUCKER_KIDS/29-BKS-TUCKER_KIDS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/29/books/review/29-BKS-TUCKER_KIDS/29-BKS-TUCKER_KIDS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/29/books/review/29-BKS-TUCKER_KIDS/29-BKS-TUCKER_KIDS-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A 12-Year-Old Gymnast Heals After a Coach’s Sexual Abuse', 'kicker': 'Children’s Books', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A 12-Year-Old Gymnast Heals After a Coach’s Sexual Abuse', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Chirp (Book)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Messner, Kate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-27T15:46:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laura Tucker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laura', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tucker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4da5940a-6d61-56ce-b6a5-8beb800f2e4d', 'word_count': 636, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4da5940a-6d61-56ce-b6a5-8beb800f2e4d'}, {'abstract': 'He’s a nominee in perpetual waiting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/27/opinion/sunday/coronavirus-trump-polls-approval.html', 'snippet': 'He’s a nominee in perpetual waiting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every day, at the White House briefing about the coronavirus, Donald Trump gets the undivided attention of the media, a national television audience bloated by crisis and as many minutes as he wants to play a “wartime president,” as he grandiosely calls himself. Never mind that he flu