parenting/kids-asking-questions-development.html', 'snippet': 'Your kid’s constant questions might be annoying but they offer a unique chance to shape their developing brains', 'lead_paragraph': 'I hopped diagonally from one fallen leaf to another, hearing them crinkle under my little 3-year-old feet. I suddenly stopped dead in my tracks, my eyes wide. “Mama, why do flowers have petals?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'If Your Kid Keeps Asking ‘Why,’ Give Them an Answer', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Intelligence and Intelligence Tests (IQ)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-27T16:23:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Parenting', 'section_name': 'Parenting', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neha Chaudhary', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chaudhary', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9173b6bb-3a8a-521e-9c08-6549635f0b89', 'word_count': 997, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9173b6bb-3a8a-521e-9c08-6549635f0b89'}, {'abstract': 'More con artists are finding their marks on all manner of social media platforms, knowing that the payoff from older victims can be big.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/27/well/elderly-romance-scam.html', 'snippet': 'More con artists are finding their marks on all manner of social media platforms, knowing that the payoff from older victims can be big.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ellen Floren was not looking for love.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times',