'Well', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/131b55c4-547d-56f5-b3d6-5920b3693995', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/131b55c4-547d-56f5-b3d6-5920b3693995'}, {'abstract': 'If food is a way to show love, then in this moment, so is cleaning.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/27/opinion/coronavirus-housecleaning.html', 'snippet': 'If food is a way to show love, then in this moment, so is cleaning.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When my self-isolation began two weeks ago, I realized I needed to get honest with myself. I was not going to be a person who emerged from quarantine having discovered a new scientific theory or learned a new language. I could try to maintain some semblance of normalcy. I could write. I could cook. And I could accomplish something extra with the additional time at home. I could clean.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/27/opinion/27Weiner/27Weiner-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 612, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/27/opinion/27Weiner/27Weiner-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 612}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/27/opinion/27Weiner/27Weiner-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1004, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/27/opinion/27Weiner/27Weiner-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2007, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/27/opinion/27Weiner/27Weiner-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/27/opinion/27Weiner/27Weiner-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/27/opinion/27Weiner/27Weiner-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Housekeeping My Way Through the Pandemic', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hygiene and Cleanliness', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Orderliness and Clutter', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantines', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-27T19:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Weiner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weiner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/0cbdd810-42a7-5215-bb0c-ad883ae718a2', 'word_count': 1071, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0cbdd810-42a7-5215-bb0c-ad883ae718a2'}, {'abstract': 'Sports commentators and swimmers are having to get especially creative. Plus, we look at the sports weekend that would have been.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/27/sports/no-swimming-pools-no-sports-to-announce-no-problem.html', 'snippet': 'Sports commentators and swimmers are having to get especially creative. Plus, we look at the sports weekend that would have been.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a different world, we’d be talking about golf and tennis, trades and drafts, sign stealing and beanballs. In this world, we’re talking about swimmers looking for places to swim, announcers providing play-by-plays on dogs eating dinner, and soccer players posing for pregame photos while wearing masks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/27/sports/27nosports1/merlin_170759808_ac1be54c-9097-431f-9d1a-dc2b8f4478e4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 359, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/27/sports/27nosports1/merlin_170759808_ac1be54c-9097-431f-9d1a-dc2b8f4478e4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 359}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/27/sports/27nosports1/merlin_170759808_ac1be54c-9097-431f-9d1a-dc2b8f4478e4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 613, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/27/sports/27nosports1/merlin_170759808_ac1be54c-9097-431f-9d1a-dc2b8f4478e4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1227, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/27/sports/27nosports1/merlin_170759808_ac1be54c-9097-431f-9d1a-dc2b8f4478e4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/27/sports/27nosports1/merlin_170759808_ac1be54c-9097-431f-9d1a-dc2b8f4478e4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url'