e': 'Olshaker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b3ace95-8f1f-59a2-8034-4a73ba146539', 'word_count': 1124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b3ace95-8f1f-59a2-8034-4a73ba146539'}, {'abstract': 'It’s a tradition this drama critic would highly recommend to those looking for ways to find magic in empty hours.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/27/theater/plays-to-read-out-loud.html', 'snippet': 'It’s a tradition this drama critic would highly recommend to those looking for ways to find magic in empty hours.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our stage was always a sofa — the long one that faced the fireplace. It could easily seat four or five, but my mother and I would huddle at one end, sunk into extra cushions, with our books on our laps.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/27/arts/27outloud-1/27outloud-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 751, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/27/arts/27outloud-1/27outloud-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 751}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/27/arts/27outloud-1/27outloud-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 819, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/27/arts/27outloud-1/27outloud-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1638, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/27/arts/27outloud-1/27outloud-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75,