ginal': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/48b0282b-3bc9-552c-a43a-4cde9899c7bf', 'word_count': 678, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48b0282b-3bc9-552c-a43a-4cde9899c7bf'}, {'abstract': 'If you’ve had to cancel a fertility treatment because of coronavirus, we’d like to hear from you. Please fill out this form.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/27/us/has-coronavirus-affected-your-fertility-treatments-tell-us-your-concerns.html', 'snippet': 'If you’ve had to cancel a fertility treatment because of coronavirus, we’d like to hear from you. Please fill out this form.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the coronavirus pandemic has worsened, the American Society for Reproductive Medicine (A.S.R.M.) issued new guidelines on March 17, advising its more than 8,000 members to avoid starting new treatment cycles for I.V.F., IUI and egg freezing; consider canceling embryo transfers; and suspend all nonemergency surgeries. It made an exception for patients who have urgent needs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Has Coronavirus Affected Your Fertility Treatments? Tell Us Your Concerns.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infertility', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Egg Donation and Freezing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Childbirth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fertility Drugs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN SOCIETY FOR REPRODUCTIVE MEDICINE', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-27T23:14:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38105f4a-8135-5156-a657-3f94adfdd51c', 'word_count': 123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38105f4a-8135-5156-a657-3f94adfdd51c'}, {'abstract': 'We’d like to hear your concerns about bearing a child during the coronavirus pandemic. Please fill out our brief form, and a reporter may respond to you.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/27/us/are-you-pregnant-and-concerned-about-coronavirus-tell-us-your-concerns.html', 'snippet': 'We’d like to hear your concerns about bearing a child during the coronavirus pandemic. Please fill out our brief form, and a reporter may respond to you.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With a lack of data on how the coronavirus may affect pregnant women, we recently found answers to expecting mothers’ most pressing questions on the pandemic. We’d like to continue to hear your concerns about bearing a child during this volatile time. Please use the form below.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Are You Pregnant and Concerned About Coronavirus? Tell Us Your Concerns.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Childbirth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-27T23:30:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/698c6186-85ea-56b1-876a-a49a207fc10c', 'word_count': 62, 'uri': 'nyt://article/698c6186-85ea-56b1-876a-a49a207fc10c'}, {'abstract': 'The White House’s coronavirus response coordinator drew criticism for comments she made about ventilator shortages, and for gushing praise of President Trump.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/27/us/politics/deborah-birx-coronavirus.html', 'snippet': 'The White House’s coronavirus response coordinator drew criticism for comments she made about ventilator shortages, and for gushing praise of President Trump.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The White House coronavirus task force has featured two trusted medical voices, diplomatic but authoritative, able to gently push back on President Trump without incurring his wrath: Drs. Anthony S. Fauci, the director of the National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases, and Deborah L. Birx, the coronavirus response coordinator.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/27/us/politics/27dc-birx1/merlin_170931078_2e976537-412f-42e0-a562-4f139399a794-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/27/us/politics/27dc-birx1/merlin_170931078_2e976537-412f-42e0-a562-4f139399a794-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/27/us/politics/27dc-birx1/merlin_170931078_2e976537-412f-42e0-a562-4f139399a794-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/27/us/politics/27dc-birx1/merlin_170931078_2e976537-412f-42e0-a562-4f139399a794-