in', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3494a560-49fb-5f97-9b5c-1e8792dea403', 'word_count': 578, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3494a560-49fb-5f97-9b5c-1e8792dea403'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Saturday, March 28, 2020.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/27/todayspaper/quotation-of-the-day-train-operator-is-killed-in-a-subway-car-blaze-officials-suspect-arson.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Saturday, March 28, 2020.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Being a motorman on a train is like being the captain of a ship. It doesn’t go down without you trying to save everyone on board.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day: Train Operator Is Killed In a Subway Car Blaze; Officials Suspect Arson', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quote of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2020-03-28T03:00:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Today’s Paper', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/83e9b9b6-cfbf-5666-993e-f77059d628ae', 'word_count': 51, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83e9b9b6-cfbf-5666-993e-f77059d628ae'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections that appeared in print on Saturday, March 28, 2020.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/27/pageoneplus/corrections-march-28-2020.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections that appeared in print on Saturday, March 28, 2020.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An article on Tuesday about public health experts’ plea to the federal government to take over the nation’s ventilator supply referred imprecisely to a study’s estimate of the need for ventilators in the United States. The study, by the Society of Critical Care Medicine, projected that there may be as many as one million people in the United States who need treatment with a ventilator over the course of the pandemic, not that the country will need 1 million ventilators over the course of the pandemic.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: March 28, 2020', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2020-03-28T03:03:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Corrections', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ec00ac1-7288-5ef0-9470-8a22c311d073', 'word_count': 242, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ec00ac1-7288-5ef0-9470-8a22c311d073'}, {'abstract': 'At least 17 states reported tallies of at least 1,000 infections. Illinois reported the first known U.S. death of an infant with the virus.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/28/world/coronavirus-live-news-updates.html', 'snippet': 'At least 17 states reported tallies of at least 1,000 infections. Illinois reported the first known U.S. death of an infant with the virus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This briefing has ended. Read live updates on the coronavirus pandemic here. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trump Says a Quarantine ‘Will Not Be Necessary’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Health and Human Services Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lamont, Ned', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York Metropolitan Area', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sweden', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kenya', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murphy, Philip D (1957- )', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-28T04:01:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66bac4ca-d12f-50b5-aafe-cc379640d61c', 'word_count': 3553, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66bac4ca-d12f-50b5-aafe-cc379640d61c'}, {'abstract': 'A thriller starring Tom Hanks airs on SundanceTV. And a family drama with Jeff Daniels comes to Criterion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/28/arts/television/whats-on-tv-saturday-captain-phillips-and-fly-away-home.html', 'snippet': 'A thriller starring Tom Hanks airs on SundanceTV. And a family drama with Jeff Daniels comes to Criterion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAPTAIN PHILLIPS (2013) 9 p.m. on SundanceTV. Directed by Paul Greengrass, who quickened the pace of several Bourne franchise movies, “Captain Phillips” is fraught with urgency. It’s a thriller — enhanced by its basis in true events — about an American cargo ship captain whose vessel is taken over by Somali pirates. The captain, Richard Phillips, is played by Tom Hanks, who “can convey a sense of old-fashioned American decency just by standing in the frame,” Manohla Dargis wrote in her review for The New York Times. But underneath the plot’s fast-paced action and Phillips’s all-American heroism, the movie succeeds in its humanization of the Somalis, providing “an unsettling look at global capitalism and American privilege and power,” Dargis wrote.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/28/arts/28tvcol-02/28tvcol-02-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/28/arts/28tvcol-02/28tvcol-02-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/28/arts/28tvcol-02/28tvcol-02-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/28/arts/28tvcol-02/28tvcol-02-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/28/arts/28tvcol-02/28tvcol-02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/28/arts/28tvcol-02/28tvcol-02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/28/arts/28tvcol-02/28tvcol-02-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Saturday: ‘Captain Phillips’ and ‘Fly Away Home