m-coburn-dead.html', 'snippet': 'His prolific use of a bill-blocking measure earned him his nickname, but he also won grudging respect on Capitol Hill as a political maverick.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tom Coburn, an ultraconservative Oklahoma Republican and family physician who in 16 years in Congress crusaded for limited government, using a rule-book technicality to block so many bills that frustrated legislators called him “Dr. No,” died on Saturday in Tulsa. He was 72.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/29/obituaries/29Coburn-print1/merlin_9677485_6a57d008-66ad-43f3-b09d-9c1d79605c25-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 413, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/29/obituaries/29Coburn-print1/merlin_9677485_6a57d008-66ad-43f3-b09d-9c1d79605c25-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 413}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/29/obituaries/29Coburn-print1/merlin_9677485_6a57d008-66ad-43f3-b09d-9c1d79605c25-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 704, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/29/obituaries/29Coburn-print1/merlin_9677485_6a57d008-66ad-43f3-b09d-9c1d79605c25-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1146, 'width': 1666, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/29/obituaries/29Coburn-print1/00Coburn1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/29/obituaries/29Coburn-print1/00Coburn1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thu