 'glocations', 'value': 'New York Metropolitan Area', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-29T04:04:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/427564c0-5fd5-50c1-8810-04937d2eda82', 'word_count': 3455, 'uri': 'nyt://article/427564c0-5fd5-50c1-8810-04937d2eda82'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Sunday, March 29, 2020.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/29/todayspaper/quotation-of-the-day-driving-the-long-haul-and-sensing-a-slowdown.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Sunday, March 29, 2020.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I live in something smaller than a jail cell all the time. I hear other people complaining and I’m like, get over it. There’s a lot of us living like this all the time, coronavirus or not.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day: Driving the Long Haul, and Sensing a Slowdown', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quote of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2020-03-29T04:16:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Today’s Paper', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/daf10be4-b789-5cc4-badc-c00c38e67fb7', 'word_count': 57, 'uri': 'nyt://article/daf10be4-b789-5cc4-badc-c00c38e67fb7'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections that appeared in print on Sunday, March 29, 2020.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/29/pageoneplus/corrections-march-29-2020.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections that appeared in print on Sunday, March 29, 2020.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A picture caption with an article on Page 32 about the Stellenbosch Triennale misidentified a member of the Asafo Black collective from Ghana. He is Jeffrey Otoo, not Daniel Mensah.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: March 29, 2020', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2020-03-29T04:16:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Corrections', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eab3aace-213f-5043-a971-7125eebfae93', 'word_count': 129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eab3aace-213f-5043-a971-7125eebfae93'}, {'abstract': 'Watch a tender romance on Hulu, or try out a new sitcom from Tim Heidecker and Eric Wareheim.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/29/arts/television/whats-on-tv-sunday-portrait-of-a-lady-on-fire-and-beef-house.html', 'snippet': 'Watch a tender romance on Hulu, or try out a new sitcom from Tim Heidecker and Eric Wareheim.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PORTRAIT OF A LADY ON FIRE (2019) Stream on Hulu. Much of this moving love story from the filmmaker Céline Sciamma is told through intense gazes and delicate gestures. Marianne (Noémie Merlant), an artist in 18th-century France, is commissioned to paint a portrait of Héloïse (Adèle Haenel), a lonely noblewoman who is soon to be married off. The portrait is a gift for Héloïse’s future husband, but she is dreading the wedding and refuses to sit for the painting. So her mother hires Marianne as a companion and asks her to create the artwork in secret after observing Héloïse’s every move. Her looks don’t go unnoticed. The more time Héloïse and Marianne spend alone, the deeper they fall into a passionate affair. The main draw here is the romance, but the movie is also a tale of sisterhood: an examination of women breaking free from the shackles of tradition, class and patriarchy.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/29/arts/29tvcol-portrait/29tvcol-portrait-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 316, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/29/arts/29tvcol-portrait/29tvcol-portrait-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 316}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/29/arts/29tvcol-portrait/29tvcol-portrait-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 540, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/29/arts/29tvcol-portrait/29tvcol-portrait-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1080, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/29/arts/29tvcol-portrait/29tvcol-portrait-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/29/arts/29tvcol-portrait/29tvcol-portrait-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/29/arts/29tvcol-portrait/29tvcol-portrait-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Sunday: ‘Portrait of a Lady on Fire’ and ‘Beef House’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Sunday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-29T05:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sara Aridi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Aridi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d368ac0-bed3-5f75-b006-3b76b8d226f9', 'word_count': 486, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d368ac0-bed3-5f75-b006-3b76b8d226f9'}, {'abstract': 'The sudden shutdown of businesses has upended the lives of millions of migrant laborers in Indian cities. More than a dozen migrants have died, and anger is rising.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/29/world/asia/coronavirus-india-migrants.html', 'snippet': 'The sudden shutdown of businesses has upended the lives of millions of migrant laborers in Indian cities. More than a dozen migrants have died, and anger is rising.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — In one of the biggest migrations in India’s modern history, hundreds of thousands of migrant laborers have begun long journeys on foot to get home, having been rendered homeless and jobless by Prime Minister Narendra Modi’s nationwide lockdown to contain the spread of the coronavirus.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/29/world/29virus-india1/merlin_171069630_bdefe6fd-682e-47ee-8ca4-5cfd8cbf7330-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/29/world/29virus-india1/merlin_171069630_bdefe6fd-682e-47ee-8ca4-5cfd8cbf7330-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/29/world/29virus-india1/merlin_171069630_bdefe6fd-682e-47ee-8c