erable to the coronavirus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MEXICO CITY — His clientele had all but disappeared since the Mexican government told people to stay home. And he knew he was running the risk of contracting the coronavirus himself.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/26/world/26mexico-laborers/26mexico-laborers-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/26/world/26mexico-laborers/26mexico-laborers-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/26/world/26mexico-laborers/26mexico-laborers-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/26/world/26mexico-laborers/26mexico-laborers-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/26/world/26mexico-laborers/26mexico-laborers-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/03/26/world/26mexico-laborers/26mexico-laborers-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/26/world/26mexico-laborers/26mexico-laborers-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘I Can’t Stop’: In Vast Informal Economy, Pandemic Adds to Pressure', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Crisis Batters Region’s Already Fragile Informal Economies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Street Vendors (Non-Food)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lopez Obrador, Andres Manuel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Latin America', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-30T13:54:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kirk Semple and Natalie Kitroeff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kirk', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Semple', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Natalie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kitroeff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed99704b-d05d-503b-a0fe-ce3c9a619ed7', 'word_count': 1209, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed99704b-d05d-503b-a0fe-ce3c9a619ed7'}, {'abstract': 'Step away for half an hour today, if you can, and make yourself a turkey and apple sandwich, an easy pea soup or an omelet, using Jacques Pépin’s technique.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/30/dining/you-deserve-a-good-lunch.html', 'snippet': 'Step away for half an hour today, if you can, and make yourself a turkey and apple sandwich, an easy pea soup or an omelet, using Jacques Pépin’s technique.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning. Here we go again with the screens and the earphones, another day on the uncomfortable chair, the dog at my feet. The commute wasn’t bad, though, and there was a beautiful, orange-yolked egg for breakfast, nestled in a piece of toast — what some call a Guy Kibbee, after the actor, who made the dish in a film — and a tall glass of cold-brewed coffee to go with it. Pretty grand.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/12/21/dining/21COOKING_PEASOUP2/21COOKING_PEASOUP2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/12/21/dining/21COOKING_PEASOUP2/21COOKING_PEASOUP2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/12/21/dining/21COOKING_PEASOUP2/21COOKING_PEASOUP2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/12/21/dining/21COOKING_PEASOUP2/21COOKING_PEASOUP2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/12/21/dining/21COOKING_PEASOUP2/21COOKING_PEASOUP2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/12/21/dining/21COOKING_PEASOUP2/21COOKING_PEASOUP2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/12/21/dining/21COOKING_PEASOUP2/21COOKING_PEASOUP2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'