taurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Trucks and Vendors', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chefs', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-30T20:25:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Wells', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wells', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65c00b09-513c-571a-a85b-787f54c1afe2', 'word_count': 1628, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65c00b09-513c-571a-a85b-787f54c1afe2'}, {'abstract': 'Even a single one is worth offering for donation. But call a health department or look online for drop-off specifics — don’t bring them to a hospital.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/30/magazine/how-to-donate-n95-masks-coronavirus.html', 'snippet': 'Even a single one is worth offering for donation. But call a health department or look online for drop-off specifics — don’t bring them to a hospital.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Giving a mask to a health care provider on the front line has more potential for a positive impact than wearing it around the grocery store,” says Conrad Amenta, director of policy and strategic initiatives at the California Academy of Family Physicians, which represents some 11,000 family doctors. Many of them have recently said they were running out of supplies and would welcome donations of personal protective equipment, including face shields, surgical gowns, nonlatex gloves, sanitizing gel and especially respirator-type N95 masks. “Please don’t just go walking into a hospital trying to drop them off,” Amenta says.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/05/magazine/05Mag-Tip-01/05Mag-Tip-01-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 613, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/04/05/magazine/05Mag-Tip-01/05Mag-Tip-01-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 613}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/05/magazine/05Mag-Tip-01/05Mag-Tip-01-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 808, 'width': 791, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/05/magazine/05Mag-Tip-01/05Mag-Tip-01-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 808, 'width': 791, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/05/magazine/05Mag-Tip-01/05Mag-Tip-01-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/04/05/magazine/05Mag-Tip-01/05Mag-Tip-01-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/05/magazine/05Mag-Tip-01/05Mag-Tip-01-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Donate N95 Masks', 'kicker': 'Tip ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How to Donate N95 Masks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Masks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Protective Clothing and Gear', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-30T20:27:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Malia Wollan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Malia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wollan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f0488df-2765-5868-950e-2acf0ca50d67', 'word_count': 353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f0488df-2765-5868-950e-2acf0ca50d67'}, {'abstract': 'On her run, she finished a six-mile loop with no trouble, but she felt a little off: a bit of chest tightness, a headache. Was this coronavirus?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/30/magazine/covid-19-symptoms-doctor.html', 'snippet': 'On her run, she finished a six-mile loop with no trouble, but she felt a little off: a bit of chest tightness, a headache. Was this coronavirus?', 'lead_paragraph': '“I don’t know what you’re feeling,” the supervising doctor said over the phone, his voice calm and reassuring. “But based on the text you sent me, you shouldn’t go to work.” The 29-year-old woman, an anesthesiology resident in her second year of training, breathed a sigh of relief. “Now,” the training-program director continued, “tell me what’s going on.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/05/magazine/05mag-diagnosis1/05mag-diagnosis1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 477, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/04/05/magazine/05mag-diagnosis1/05mag-diagnosis1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 477}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'typ