, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Our Family Haggadah (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Asher, Spring', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-31T00:33:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dfd84c4c-59e3-5c80-aef7-bdd094f7a41a', 'word_count': 118, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dfd84c4c-59e3-5c80-aef7-bdd094f7a41a'}, {'abstract': 'A limited-edition tool from Victorinox, the makers of Swiss Army knives, combines a santoku blade with Middle Eastern-style steel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/30/dining/victorinox-damast-knife.html', 'snippet': 'A limited-edition tool from Victorinox, the makers of Swiss Army knives, combines a santoku blade with Middle Eastern-style steel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s not your typical Swiss Army knife. Victorinox, the company that makes those gadget-laden implements, also has several lines of simpler kitchen cutlery. Its newest is a cross-cultural affair, made with a Japanese santoku-shaped seven-inch blade instead of a standard chef’s knife blade. It’s called Damast because the steel is forged according to the Damascus technique originally used for swords in the Middle East. That approach makes the blade both strong and flexible, and has a typically wavy pattern. The knife, a limited edition, has a comfortable walnut handle and is well balanced.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/01/dining/30burner-knife/merlin_171046905_63a9cffc-5137-4533-802a-87b585683b98-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 650, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/04/01/dining/30burner-knife/merlin_171046905_63a9cffc-5137-4533-802a-87b585683b98-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 650}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/01/dining/30burner-knife/merlin_171046905_63a9cffc-5137-4533-802a-87b585683b98-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 946, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/01/dining/30burner-knife/merlin_171046905_63a9cffc-5137-4533-802a-87b585683b98-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1892, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/01/dining/30burner-knife/30burner-knife-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/04/01/dining/30burner-knife/30burner-knife-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/01/dining/30burner-knife/30burner-knife-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Knife to Add Flash to Your Kitchen', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Use: Flashy Knives For Your Kitchen', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Knives', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Victorinox AG', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cookware', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-31T00:35:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e93bfe6-78aa-54b3-92d2-cde11999173c', 'word_count': 124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e93bfe6-78aa-54b3-92d2-cde11999173c'}, {'abstract': 'Bona Furtuna’s line, made in the town of Corleone, includes antipasti and marinara sauces.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/30/dining/pasta-sauce.html', 'snippet': 'Bona Furtuna’s line, made in the town of Corleone, includes antipasti and marinara sauces.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though the name Corleone may be best known from “The Godfather,” Corleone is also a town near Palermo, Sicily, that is the source of some ancient grains used to make pasta, heirloom tomatoes for sauce and thousand-year-old olive trees for oil for a company based there, Bona Furtuna. Its pastas are particularly flavorful without being heavy. The marinara sauces include one that’s seductively fragrant with oregano flowers. There are also jarred chiles stuffed with tuna and olives for antipasto. Some of the profits go to charities in Sicily and the United States. Through April 15, they are donating 20 percent of online sales to No Kid Hungry and Banco Alimentare.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/01/dining/30burner-Bona/30burner-Bona-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 645, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/04/01/dining/30burner-Bona/30burner-Bona-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 645}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/01/dining/30burner-Bona/30burner-Bona-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 954, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/01/dining/30burner-Bona/30burner-Bona-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1747, 'width': 1626, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/01/dining/30burner-Bona/30burner-Bona-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/04/01/dining/30burner-Bona/30burner-Bona-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/01/dining/30burner-Bona/30burner-Bona-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tempting Pastas and Sauces From Sicily', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Cook: Pastas and Sauces That Are Hard to Refuse', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pasta', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sauces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bona Furtuna LLC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-31T00:36:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d3998f9-4ad6-5b32-ac8e-d275137cef30', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d3998f9-4ad6-5b32-ac8e-d275137cef30'}, {'abstract': 'Grimaldi’s Pizzeria is delivering pies from Brooklyn, or order frozen pizzas from Naples, Italy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/30/dining/grimaldis-pizza-delivery-coronavirus.html', 'snippet': 'Grimaldi’s Pizzeria is delivering pies from Brooklyn, or order frozen pizzas from Naples, Italy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It took a virus. For the first time in its more than 100-year history, the original Grimaldi’s Pizzeria is delivering its coal-oven pizzas with online ordering available. Pizzas can be also be picked up at the restaurant. Traditional, white and pesto pizzas are on the menu along with calzones, some antipasti like Caesar salad and desserts. But assuming Dumbo isn’t so convenient for those living in St. Louis, say, or Miami, or even the Bronx, how about Naples, Italy, for pizza, without getting on a plane? Excellent flash-frozen pizzas shipped directly from Naples, which were first sold in New York a year ago, are now available for delivery nationwide. The 11-inch pizzas, from Talia di Napoli, come with assorted toppings, and also plain or just cheese for your own creations. Eight to 10 minutes in the oven is all it takes to go from freezer to table.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/01/dining/30burner-pizza/30burner-pizza-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/04/01/dining/30burner-pizza/30burner-pizza-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/01/dining/30burner-pizza/30burner-pizza-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/01/dining/30burner-pizza/30burner-pizza-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1361, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/01/dining/30burner-pizza/30burner-pizza-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/04/01/dining/30burner-pizza/30burner-pizza-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/01/dining/30burner-pizza/30burner-pizza-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Your Quarantine Pizza Cravings', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Serve: I’m Craving Pizza. Dumbo or Naples?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pizza', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Grimaldi's Pizzeria", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Victus LLC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantines', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dumbo (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Naples (Italy)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-31T00:40:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0b0f5b0-c22b-53f9-82ba-105c9c6265f5', 'word_count': 206, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0b0f5b0-c22b-53f9-82ba-105c9c6265f5'}, {'abstract': 'AndSons, from the chocolatier Kriss Harvey, sells colorful chocolate eggs filled with layers of sweet goodness.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/30/dining/and-sons-easter-egg.html', 'snippet': 'AndSons, from the chocolatier Kriss Harvey, sells colorful chocolate eggs filled with layers of sweet goodness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What would Easter be without fanciful chocolate eggs? These, from andSons, a chocolate shop with pedigree that opened last spring in Beverly Hills, Calif., appear simple, colorful and unadorned, but inside they’re a confectioner’s dreamscape. Layers of peanut nougat, pecan praline, chocolate marshmallow, yuzu ganache and vanilla caramel, among other components fill the various molded, colorful eggs. The chocolatier is Kriss Harvey, who was the executive pastry chef for José Andrés’s restaurant the Bazaar in Los Angeles. The shop is owned by Marc and Phil Covitz, in the spot where their mother, Aviva, had a Swiss chocolate shop.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/01/dining/30burner-egg/30burner-egg-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 335, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/04/01/dining/30burner-egg/30burner-egg-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 335}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/01/dining/30burner-egg/30burner-egg-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 571, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/01/dining/30burner-egg/30burner-egg-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1116, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/01/dining/30burner-egg/30burner-egg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/04/01/dining/30burner-egg/30burner-egg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/01/dining/30burner-egg/30burner-egg-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Easter Egg From Beverly Hills', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Gift: An Easter Egg From California', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Easter and Holy Week', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chocolate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AndSons (Beverly Hills, Calif, Retailer)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-31T00:43:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/123c3ec0-3c93-567d-9f89-979eb2bbc1d6', 'word_count': 138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/123c3ec0-3c93-567d-9f89-979eb2bbc1d6'}, {'abstract': 'The Pickle Guys sell white and red horseradish for your Seder plate or to pair with gefilte fish.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/30/dining/pickle-guys-horseradish.html', 'snippet': 'The Pickle Guys sell white and red horseradish for your Seder plate or to pair with gefilte fish.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The bitter herb or moror, for the Seder plate is usually horseradish (in my home, slivers of the fresh root). I’m not sure I’ll be shopping for it this year, but the jarred kind is always a substitute. And it’s a standard accompaniment for gefilte fish. Freshly made, properly forceful white (plain) and red (beet) horseradish is available from the Pickle Guys on the Lower East Side. It’s kosher for Passover. And this year it can be ordered for nationwide shipping, as well as curbside pickup.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/01/dining/30burner-horse/30burner-horse-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/04/01/dining/30burner-horse/30burner-horse-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 480}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/01/dining/30burner-horse/30burner-horse-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/01/dining/30burner-horse/30burner-horse-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1638, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/01/dining/30burner-horse/30burner-horse-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/04/01/dining/30burner-horse/30burner-horse-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 