9-5c64-970c-557652b251d0'}, {'abstract': 'How caregivers can use technology to help older people minimize going to the doctor during this pandemic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/31/well/family/coronavirus-elderly-caregivers.html', 'snippet': 'How caregivers can use technology to help older people minimize going to the doctor during this pandemic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the United States today, there are approximately four million older adults who are not in nursing facilities but who need help with personal care (bathing, dressing or eating) and another 3.5 million older adults who need assistance in areas such as finances and cooking to live independently. These older adults depend on caregivers, either paid home health aides or unpaid family members, for their day-to-day existence. Both family caregivers and those they care for need to rapidly adapt if they are to remain safe during the coronavirus epidemic.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/30/well/00well-caregivers/00well-caregivers-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/30/well/00well-caregivers/00well-caregivers-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/30/well/00well-caregivers/00well-caregivers-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/30/well/00well-caregivers/00well-caregivers-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 837, 'width': 1254, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit'