rge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/31/sports/31fifa1/31fifa1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'FIFA Plans Huge Emergency Fund to Support Ailing Soccer Industry', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In a Shutdown, It Could Be FIFA to the Rescue', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Federation of Association Football (FIFA)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Finances', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-31T12:03:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tariq Panja', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tariq', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Panja', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b84bb8c-c4df-5df0-a618-a716749c6934', 'word_count': 1048, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b84bb8c-c4df-5df0-a618-a716749c6934'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. dePaola wrote or illustrated more than 270 books, notably the beloved stories of a “grandma witch” with an eternally full pasta pot.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/31/books/tomie-de-paola-dead.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. dePaola wrote or illustrated more than 270 books, notably the beloved stories of a “grandma witch” with an eternally full pasta pot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tomie dePaola, the celebrated author and illustrator whose scores of children’s books nurtured and delighted several generations of readers, died on Monday in Lebanon, N.H. He was 85.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/02/world/31depaola-obituary/merlin_171128568_15722b79-6bdc-4ca3-8928-cd9d27b9e21c-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/04/02/world/31depaola-obituary/merlin_171128568_15722b79-6bdc-4ca3-8928-cd9d27b9e21c-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/02/world/31depaola-obituary/merlin_171128568_15722b79-6bdc-4ca3-8928-cd9d27b9e21c-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/02/world/31depaola-obituary/merlin_171128568_15722b79-6bdc-4ca3-8928-cd9d27b9e21c-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/02/world/31depaola-obituary/31depaola-obituary-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2020/04/02/world/31depaola-obituary/31depaola-obituary-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/04/02/world/31depaola-obituary/31depaola-obituary-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tomie dePaola, ‘Strega Nona’ Author and Illustrator, Dies at 85', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tomie dePaola, 85, Dies; His ‘Strega Nona’ Books Captivated Children', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DePaola, Tomie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Strega Nona (Book)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-31T12:16:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Obits', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Iliana Magra and Julia Carmel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Iliana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Magra', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carmel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/7566c09b-45b6-51ac-90bc-5782d64d35f9', 'word_count': 807, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7566c09b-45b6-51ac-90bc-5782d64d35f9'}, {'abstract': 'An excerpt from “Sharks in the Time of Saviors,” by Kawai Strong Washburn', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/31/books/review/sharks-in-the-time-of-saviors-by-kawai-strong-washburn-an-excerpt.html', 'snippet': 'An excerpt from “Sharks in the Time of Saviors,” by Kawai Strong Washburn', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I close my eyes we’re all still alive and it becomes obvious then what the gods want from us. The myth people tell about us might start on that liquid blue day off Kona and the sharks, but I know different. We started earlier. You started earlier. The kingdom of Hawai‘i had long been broken—the breathing rain forests and singing green reefs crushed under the haole fists of beach resorts and skyscrapers—and that was when the land had begun calling. I know this now because of you. And that the gods were hungry for change and you were that change. In our first days I saw so many signs, but didn’t believe. The first came when your father and I were naked in his pickup truck in Waipi‘o Valley, and we witnessed the night marchers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Sharks in the Time of Saviors,’ by Kawai Strong Washburn: An Excerpt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2020-03-31T12:43:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b82a7e39-3058-55e9-99a4-201e0e5b77c0', 'word_count': 2089, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b82a7e39-3058-55e9-99a4-201e0e5b77c0'}, {'abstract': 'Tuesday: The state hopes to add scores of additional health care workers as hospitals fill. Also: Easy California history lessons.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/31/us/california-health-corps-newsom.html', 'snippet': 'Tuesday: The state hopes to add scores of additional health care workers as hospitals fill. Also: Easy California history lessons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/31/us/31hospitalscatoday/merlin_171128151_dc99c14f-3e1e-4247-9335-e9c0846e4fc2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/31/us/31hospitalscatoday/merlin_171128151_dc99c14f-3e1e-4247-9335-e9c0846e4fc2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/31/us/31hospitalscatoday/merlin_171128151