 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aircraft Carriers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Navy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guam', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vietnam', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2020-03-31T15:01:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Gibbons-Neff and Helene Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gibbons-Neff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Helene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa2fc26a-66e9-5ff4-92ab-301875cd0c60', 'word_count': 1042, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa2fc26a-66e9-5ff4-92ab-301875cd0c60'}, {'abstract': 'An excerpt from “August,” by Callan Wink', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/31/books/review/august-by-callan-wink-an-excerpt.html', 'snippet': 'An excerpt from “August,” by Callan Wink', 'lead_paragraph': 'August flew back to Michigan for Thanksgiving. It was his first time on an airplane, and even though he tried to be nonchalant about it, he held his breath during takeoff and let it out loud enough after they were finally airborne that his seatmate looked at him sidelong. His father met him at the airport in Grand Rapids. He shook August’s hand and threw his bag in the back of his truck, and they started the drive north.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘August,’ by Callan Wink: An Excerpt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2020-03-31T15:20:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/28daff27-6632-537c-ad9d-2a1d38fc5288', 'word_count': 2776, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28daff27-6632-537c-ad9d-2a1d38fc5288'}, {'abstract': 'The health crisis, which has become a fresh test of survival for a country where life has been a daily fight for decades, has provoked a shared sense of responsibility and spontaneous acts of generosity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2020/03/31/world/asia/coronavirus-afghanistan-kindness.html', 'snippet': 'The health crisis, which has become a fresh test of survival for a country where life has been a daily fight for decades, has provoked a shared sense of responsibility and spontaneous acts of generosity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — Around the time his hometown turned into the epicenter of coronavirus in Afghanistan and the government began a lockdown, Mohamed Kareem Tawain, an 80-year-old dentist in the western city of Herat, had a dream one night: that he took some money from his wife to distribute for charity, but found no one on the streets to give it to.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2020/03/31/world/31virus-afghan-gernerosity/merlin_170667594_e93b428f-2607-429b-80bd-1edc63369946-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2020/03/31/world/31virus-afghan-gernerosity/merlin_170667594_e93b428f-2607-429b-80bd-1edc633